## 24. The lecturer's research run

Reframe recorded on 9 October 2026 at the owner's request. Lyceum is not a set of agents that run continuously. It is a workspace in which a lecturer does what a careful lecturer would do anyway, faster and with receipts:

1. **Search.** Choose a source with a stated policy (today: the Greenhouse and Lever employer board APIs, fetched on request through the local API, or a dated saved sample), enter the roles graduates apply to, fetch, and keep the postings worth reading. Each kept posting becomes a source with its link, publication date as published, retrieval time and text fingerprint.
2. **Read.** Name the skills that matter, in the lecturer's words. The scan proposes the sentence in each posting that uses a term; the lecturer confirms each quotation, and a paraphrase is rejected by the citation validator. The lecturer then vouches that the extraction is complete, and only then does the posting count.
3. **See the trend.** Observed requirements show the numerator and denominator, the share, a 95% Wilson interval, required against preferred wording, employers, and the course's reviewed coverage stage against its target. Empty evidence is unknown, and no trend over time is shown until a comparable earlier window exists.
4. **Decide what to do about it.** Map a skill to an outcome, record the stage with cited course evidence, and choose between keeping the course unchanged, a small refresh within existing hours, or a formal revision.
5. **Take it to the meeting.** Prepare a meeting brief with the decision requested, the evidence base, the table, the options, the lecturer's notes, the limitations and every receipt. Download it as Markdown, or send it to a colleague inside Lyceum, where it arrives on their Home page with the receipts attached.

Implemented on 9 October: all five steps, in Course Studio under Evidence and on the Home page for recipients. Proofs cover the collector (host allow-list, token validation, one-hour cache, rate limits, size and timeout limits, payload normalisation), the scan (exact substrings, requirement heuristic, no double counting), bulk review, briefs, notifications and backups. The self-driving demo plays this storyline on the saved sample. Live fetches were verified on 9 October against the Stripe board on Greenhouse (727 postings, 8 "data analyst" titles) and the Palantir site on Lever (313 postings).

Still pending from Section 7: Scrapling page adapters for approved employer pages, snapshots of arbitrary sites, cross-site vacancy clustering, scheduled refresh with refresh-failure reporting, and contextual sources beyond manual paste. The seven branded agents remain product labels for roles in this workflow; none of them runs on its own.

What changed in the claims: Lyceum no longer says that agents monitor the market. It says that the lecturer runs a research run when a decision needs one, and that every number can be traced to a quotation the lecturer confirmed.

## 25. Lyceum inside the tools universities already use

The owner's commercial question: a university already has an LMS, Teams or Slack, a curriculum system and a dozen other tools, so why add one more? The answer the plan now takes: do not ask them to. Lyceum should be reachable from the tools they already open, with the web workspace kept for the work that needs a full editor.

| Surface | Good for | Poor at | Needs |
|---|---|---|---|
| Web workspace (today) | Editing outlines, confirming quotations, reviewing tables, preparing briefs | Nothing it does better elsewhere | The local API for live boards |
| Microsoft Teams and Microsoft 365 Copilot through a Copilot Studio agent | Asking what employers want in a role, receiving a brief in a channel, escalating to a coordinator, approvals in chat | Editing an outline; confirming dozens of quotations; anything that needs a table with controls | Copilot Studio reaches external systems through a custom connector or a REST API tool defined from an OpenAPI description, with Entra ID sign-in; publishing to Teams goes through the Channels page and admin approval |
| Slack app | The same conversational asks and escalations in Slack-first universities | The same editing limits | A small Slack app with slash commands and link unfurls over the same API |
| LMS through LTI 1.3 | Launching the course workspace from the course page; sharing a brief as course material | Institution-wide analytics | An LMS test site and administrator configuration |

The shared piece is one small API over a shared store: collect a board, list evidence, produce a report or brief, send a brief, record a decision. That API is the W02 server work, which now has a concrete reason to exist. Sequencing stays as decided: local-first for the competition demo, the shared API and identity when a pilot has a date, then the Teams or Slack surface for the pilot institution's actual tool.

Efficiency and performance differ by surface, and the pitch should say so: the chat surfaces are for asking and escalating, the workspace is for editing and confirming, and the file exports keep working everywhere. Copilot Studio also carries licensing and admin-approval steps that the institution's IT team controls; these are costs of adoption, not features. Nothing in this section is implemented yet. It is the integration strategy and the commercial answer to "why another tool". Sources are in Section 29.

## 26. Pitch structure: the AWS five V's

The owner asked for the five V framing seen in an AWS presentation. The closest published framework is the AWS Machine Learning Blog's five V's for taking AI projects from pilot to production (24 October 2025): Value, Visualize, Validate, Verify, Venture. It is a delivery framework rather than an investor template, which suits a technology-readiness jury. The mapping:

| V | The framework's question | Lyceum's answer, with evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Value | Is this worth solving? | Lecturers must refresh courses against employer demand and defend the change to colleagues and reviewers; today the evidence lives in browser tabs and memory. Malaysian graduates face a persistent qualification-to-job mismatch (DOSM reports 32.2% underemployment among graduates in 2024), and MOHE reviews courses for relevance. The pain is felt by lecturers, coordinators and quality units. |
| Visualize | How will we know it worked? | The pilot measures in Section 17: task completion, time to an accepted brief, zero fabricated citations in a checked sample, review effort, repeat use. Baselines come from the lecturer's current process. |
| Validate | How do we build it? | Built and checked: on-request collection from two documented board APIs, the exact-quotation validator, honest denominators, briefs and escalation; 149 automated checks, four browser smokes and a self-driving demo on a dated sample of real postings. No model key is required for any of it. |
| Verify | How do we run it at scale? | Local-first today; a shared API and identity when a pilot has a date; Teams or Slack surfaces through that API; source policies, retention and audit records designed in from the start. |
| Venture | How do we fund it through to value? | Near-zero variable cost for the deterministic path; optional AI and media behind caps; a department pilot before any institution licence; the market sizing in Section 27. The ask is a pilot with 3 to 5 lecturers. |

Use the five V's as the deck's spine when the audience is a readiness or innovation jury. Keep the Section 19 script when the slot is five minutes and the audience is approving a direction.

## 27. Market sizing: labelled estimates

Everything here is an estimate from public sources checked on 9 October 2026. The sources disagree on definitions, and none of them measures willingness to pay for Lyceum. Treat the figures as the shape of the market, not a forecast.

**Units.** The user is a lecturer; the buyer is a department, faculty or central teaching unit; the licence unit is most likely an institution or a department, not a seat.

| Layer | Definition | Figure and source | Caveat |
|---|---|---|---|
| TAM, world | Accredited higher education institutions and their teaching staff | Over 22,000 accredited institutions and 269 million students in 2024 (UNESCO global roadmap); over 14 million tertiary teachers (UNESCO IESALC) | Institution counts range from 18,000 to 88,000 depending on definition |
| Adjacent spend | Curriculum and catalogue management software for higher education | 2025 estimates from USD 0.48 billion to USD 3.5 billion with 7 to 9 percent annual growth (Report Prime, Dataintelo, MarketIntelo, 360iResearch) | A sevenfold spread between publishers; none isolates labour-market alignment |
| SAM, Malaysia | Lecturers and institutions reachable with a file-first tool that fits MQA course reviews | MOHE 2023 statistics: 22,370 lecturers in public universities, 19,743 in private institutions, 2,772 in polytechnics, roughly 45,000 before research fellows and assistant lecturers. Institutions: 20 public universities; 65 private universities, 38 university colleges and 252 colleges (MIDA, February 2026); polytechnics and community colleges in addition | The 2024 MOHE tables exist but the staff figures were not legible in the PDF extraction; verify against Chapter 1, Table 1.6 |
| SOM, first two years | Departments that run a pilot and convert | 3 to 5 pilot institutions, 50 to 200 lecturers, one or two paid department licences | A target, not a forecast |

**Illustrative arithmetic, not a projection.** If a department licence were priced at RM 6,000 to RM 15,000 a year and a pilot converted five departments, year-two revenue would be RM 30,000 to RM 75,000. The Malaysian ceiling at that price, across roughly 400 institutions with several departments each, is in the low millions of ringgit a year. This is why Section 25 matters: the cost of adoption must be close to zero for the market to be worth serving, and the competitive answer is to fit into existing tools rather than to add a platform.

**Competitors and positioning.** Lightcast Skillabi (alignment scores from course text against a large labour-market dataset, pricing on request), Chmura JobsEQ (programme alignment through CIP to SOC crosswalks) and the curriculum suites (Ellucian, Watermark, CourseLeaf, Modern Campus, Coursedog) sit above the lecturer: institutional licences, global datasets, scores whose formula is not published. Lyceum sits at the lecturer's desk: receipts the lecturer confirmed, denominators in view, a brief for the meeting, and a path into Teams or Slack. It can later ingest a licensed dataset as another source with a policy; it does not need to replace one. Claims of novelty stay at defensible differentiation, as Section 6 already says.

**Why now, in Malaysia.** DOSM counted 5.98 million graduates in 2024 with unemployment at 3.2 percent but underemployment at 32.2 percent; TalentCorp's MyCOL 2024/2025 lists 66 critical occupations; MOHE reviews courses for relevance. These are reasons a department would fund a pilot, not proof that it will. Sources are listed in Section 29.

## 28. Further improvements identified on 9 October

In priority order after the research run:

1. Quarantine the synthetic screens. Trends, the public Relevance Index, the Acceptance test and the Closed loop still run on fixtures from the earlier storyline. Keep them reachable for the proofs, but move them out of the lecturer's navigation behind a research sandbox label so that the first thing a judge opens is the real workflow.
2. Provider drift in W06: upgrade the Anthropic SDK, replace the forced tool call in the intake route with structured outputs, set a current model id, and surface payload truncation.
3. Comparable time windows: store each collection run as a dated window so that a later run can report a change in percentage points with both denominators, as Section 8.1 specifies.
4. Employer naming for Lever boards: the API does not state the employer, so the site token is used; allow renaming on import.
5. Brief export to DOCX and PDF in addition to Markdown, for meetings that will not open a Markdown file.
6. Code-split the bundle; the main chunk now exceeds 500 kB.
7. An accessibility pass with NVDA on the research run, which has more controls than any other section.
8. An OpenAPI description of the collect, report and brief operations, as the first artefact of the extension strategy and the contract for W02.
9. A deck in the five-V structure, a recording of the new Play demo, and a rehearsal on the presentation machine.

// The lecturer's research run: fetch postings from a permitted board on request,
// keep the ones worth reading, scan them for the skills the lecturer names,
// confirm each exact quotation, vouch for the extraction, then turn the result
// into a meeting brief that can be downloaded or sent to a colleague.

import { useState } from "react";
import {
  clearCollection, clearProposals, confirmProposals, dismissProposal, importCollectedPostings, nowIso, prepareEvidenceBrief, runCollection,
  scanForRequirements, selectBrief, sendEvidenceBrief, setSkillLexicon, setSourcesReviewed, type AppState,
} from "../../app/store.ts";
import { briefDeck, downloadDeck } from "../../lib/slides.ts";
import { BOARD_TOKEN, SOURCE_POLICIES, matchedKeywords, parseKeywords } from "../../lib/collect.ts";
import { RECOMMENDATION_LABEL, REQUIREMENT_LEVELS, evidenceReport, parseLexicon, type MentionProposal } from "../../lib/evidence.ts";
import { downloadText } from "../../lib/download.ts";
import type { BriefRecommendation, CollectionProvider, MentionRequirement, Person, Subject } from "../../types.ts";
import { Button, Field, Input, Select, Tag, Textarea } from "../primitives/index.tsx";
import { useUnsavedEditor } from "../useUnsavedEditor.ts";

type Props = { state: AppState; person: Person; subject: Subject; mayEdit: boolean };
const PROVIDERS = Object.keys(SOURCE_POLICIES) as CollectionProvider[];

export function ResearchRun({ state, subject, mayEdit }: Props) {
  const [provider, setProvider] = useState<CollectionProvider>("sample");
  const [board, setBoard] = useState("");
  const [query, setQuery] = useState("");
  const [inText, setInText] = useState(false);
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const run = state.collectRun && state.collectRun.subjectId === subject.id ? state.collectRun : null;
  const policy = SOURCE_POLICIES[provider];
  const postings = run?.status === "done" ? run.postings : [];
  const keywords = parseKeywords(run?.query ?? "");
  const imported = new Set(state.evidenceSources.filter((s) => s.subjectId === subject.id).map((s) => s.collection?.postingId ?? ""));
  const boardOk = provider === "sample" || BOARD_TOKEN.test(board.trim());
  async function fetchNow() {
    setMessage(""); setSelected([]);
    const result = await runCollection(subject.id, { provider, board, query, inText });
    if (!result.ok) setMessage(result.error);
  }
  return <section className="workspace-panel" aria-labelledby="research-run">
    <div className="section-heading"><div><h3 id="research-run">Research run</h3><p className="muted">Fetch postings from a permitted employer board when you ask, then keep the ones worth reading as evidence.</p></div></div>
    {mayEdit ? <>
      <div className="form-grid">
        <Field label="Source"><Select data-demo-id="collect-provider" value={provider} onChange={(e) => { setProvider(e.target.value as CollectionProvider); setMessage(""); }}>{PROVIDERS.map((p) => <option key={p} value={p}>{SOURCE_POLICIES[p].name}</option>)}</Select></Field>
        {provider !== "sample" ? <Field label="Employer board token" hint={provider === "greenhouse" ? "The name in boards.greenhouse.io/NAME, or in an employer's careers link." : "The name in jobs.lever.co/NAME."}><Input data-demo-id="collect-board" maxLength={80} value={board} onChange={(e) => setBoard(e.target.value)} placeholder={provider === "greenhouse" ? "e.g. stripe" : "e.g. palantir"} /></Field> : null}
        <Field label="Role keywords" hint="Comma-separated. Matches posting titles; tick the box below to search inside the text too."><Input data-demo-id="collect-query" value={query} onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)} placeholder="e.g. data analyst, analytics" /></Field>
      </div>
      <label className="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" checked={inText} onChange={(e) => setInText(e.target.checked)} />Also match keywords inside the posting text</label>
      <details className="guide-entry"><summary><span>Source policy: {policy.name}</span><Tag tone={policy.enabled ? "ok" : "warn"}>{policy.enabled ? "Permitted on request" : "Disabled"}</Tag></summary>
        <div className="guide-entry-body"><dl className="context-list"><div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>{policy.owner}</dd></div><div><dt>Method</dt><dd>{policy.method}</dd></div><div><dt>Retention</dt><dd>{policy.retention}</dd></div><div><dt>Refresh</dt><dd>{policy.refresh}</dd></div><div><dt>Policy reviewed</dt><dd>{policy.policyReviewedOn}</dd></div></dl><p className="muted">{policy.note}</p></div></details>
      <div className="button-row">
        <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="collect-run" disabled={run?.status === "running" || !boardOk} onClick={() => void fetchNow()}>{run?.status === "running" ? "Fetching..." : "Fetch postings"}</Button>
        {run ? <Button onClick={() => { clearCollection(); setSelected([]); setMessage(""); }}>Clear results</Button> : null}
      </div>
      {message ? <p role="alert" className="form-error">{message}</p> : null}
      {run ? <div data-demo-id="collect-log"><div className="button-row"><h4>Collection log</h4>{run.status === "running" ? <Tag tone="warn">Fetching now</Tag> : run.status === "failed" ? <Tag tone="danger">Failed</Tag> : run.provider === "sample" ? <Tag>Saved sample, no network</Tag> : run.cached ? <Tag tone="accent">Local cache of a live fetch</Tag> : <Tag tone="ok">Fetched live</Tag>}</div>
        <ol className="collect-log" aria-live="polite">{run.log.map((line, i) => <li key={i}>{line}</li>)}</ol></div> : null}
      {run?.status === "failed" ? <p role="alert" className="form-error">{run.error}</p> : null}
      {run?.status === "done" ? <div>
        <p role="status" className="save-status" data-demo-id="collect-status">{postings.length} of {run.total} postings match{run.query ? " \"" + run.query + "\"" : ""} on {run.label}. Retrieved {run.retrievedAt}{run.cached ? ", served from the local cache" : ""}. Publication dates are shown as published; the retrieval time is kept separately.</p>
        {postings.length ? <>
          <div className="button-row">
            <Button data-demo-id="collect-select-all" onClick={() => setSelected(postings.filter((p) => !imported.has(p.id)).map((p) => p.id))}>Select all shown</Button>
            <Button onClick={() => setSelected([])}>Clear selection</Button>
            <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="collect-import" disabled={!selected.length} onClick={() => {
              const result = importCollectedPostings(subject.id, selected);
              setMessage(result.ok ? "" : result.error);
              if (result.ok) setSelected([]);
            }}>Import {selected.length ? selected.length + " " : ""}selected as sources</Button>
          </div>
          <div className="table-scroll"><table className="evidence-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Keep</th><th scope="col">Title</th><th scope="col">Employer</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Published</th><th scope="col">Matched</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{postings.map((p) => <tr key={p.id}>
              <td><input type="checkbox" aria-label={"Keep " + p.title} data-demo-id={"collect-select-" + p.id} checked={selected.includes(p.id)} disabled={imported.has(p.id)} onChange={(e) => setSelected(e.target.checked ? [...selected, p.id] : selected.filter((id) => id !== p.id))} /></td>
              <th scope="row">{p.url ? <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{p.title}</a> : p.title}{imported.has(p.id) ? <> <Tag>Imported</Tag></> : null}</th>
              <td>{p.organisation}</td><td>{p.location || "Not stated"}</td><td className="tabular">{p.publishedAt ? p.publishedAt.slice(0, 10) : "Not supplied"}</td>
              <td>{matchedKeywords(p, keywords).join(", ") || (keywords.length ? "text only" : "all")}</td>
            </tr>)}</tbody>
          </table></div>
        </> : <p>No posting matched. Widen the keywords or search inside the text.</p>}
      </div> : null}
    </> : <p className="muted">Only assigned lecturers and coordinators can run a collection for this course.</p>}
  </section>;
}

export function RequirementScan({ state, subject, mayEdit }: Props) {
  const saved = state.skillLexicon[subject.id] ?? [];
  const [terms, setTerms] = useState(saved.join(", "));
  const [ack, setAck] = useState(false);
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const [levels, setLevels] = useState<Record<string, MentionRequirement>>({});
  const proposals = state.scanProposals.filter((p) => state.evidenceSources.some((s) => s.id === p.sourceId && s.subjectId === subject.id));
  const key = (p: MentionProposal) => p.sourceId + "\n" + p.term;
  const postings = state.evidenceSources.filter((s) => s.subjectId === subject.id && s.kind === "job-posting" && !s.duplicateOf);
  const unreviewed = postings.filter((s) => !s.reviewed);
  const dirty = JSON.stringify(parseLexicon(terms)) !== JSON.stringify(saved);
  useUnsavedEditor(dirty);
  const withLevel = (p: MentionProposal) => ({ ...p, requirement: levels[key(p)] ?? p.requirement });
  return <section className="workspace-panel" aria-labelledby="requirement-scan">
    <div className="section-heading"><div><h3 id="requirement-scan">Scan for requirements</h3><p className="muted">Name the skills you care about. The scan proposes the sentence in each posting that uses a term; you confirm every quotation.</p></div></div>
    {mayEdit ? <>
      <Field label="Skills to look for" hint="Comma-separated. Use | for an alias, for example machine learning|ML. Matching is whole-word and case-insensitive."><Textarea data-demo-id="lexicon-terms" value={terms} onChange={(e) => setTerms(e.target.value)} placeholder="e.g. SQL, Python, dashboards|dashboard, data visualisation, stakeholders|stakeholder" /></Field>
      <div className="button-row">
        <Button data-demo-id="lexicon-save" disabled={!dirty} onClick={() => { const result = setSkillLexicon(subject.id, parseLexicon(terms)); setMessage(result.ok ? "Terms saved with the course." : result.error); }}>Save terms</Button>
        <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="scan-run" disabled={dirty || !saved.length || !postings.length} onClick={() => {
          const result = scanForRequirements(subject.id);
          setMessage(result.ok ? result.count + " proposals across " + postings.length + " postings. Confirm the quotations you accept." : result.error);
          setLevels({});
        }}>Scan postings</Button>
      </div>
      {message ? <p role="status" className="save-status">{message}</p> : null}
      {proposals.length ? <>
        <div className="table-scroll"><table className="evidence-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Posting</th><th scope="col">Skill</th><th scope="col">Proposed quotation</th><th scope="col">Requirement</th><th scope="col">Decision</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{proposals.map((p) => <tr key={key(p)}>
            <th scope="row">{p.sourceTitle}</th><td>{p.skill}</td><td><blockquote className="proposal-quote">{p.excerpt}</blockquote></td>
            <td><Select aria-label={"Requirement level for " + p.skill + " in " + p.sourceTitle} value={levels[key(p)] ?? p.requirement} onChange={(e) => setLevels({ ...levels, [key(p)]: e.target.value as MentionRequirement })}>{REQUIREMENT_LEVELS.map((r) => <option key={r} value={r}>{r}</option>)}</Select></td>
            <td><div className="button-row"><Button onClick={() => confirmProposals(subject.id, [withLevel(p)])}>Confirm</Button><Button variant="quiet" onClick={() => dismissProposal(p.sourceId, p.term)}>Dismiss</Button></div></td>
          </tr>)}</tbody>
        </table></div>
        <div className="button-row">
          <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="scan-confirm-all" onClick={() => { const result = confirmProposals(subject.id, proposals.map(withLevel)); setMessage(result.added + " quotations recorded, " + result.skipped + " skipped."); }}>Confirm all {proposals.length}</Button>
          <Button onClick={() => clearProposals()}>Dismiss all</Button>
        </div>
      </> : null}
      {postings.length ? <div className="curriculum-object"><h4>Reviewed denominator</h4>
        <p className="muted">{postings.length - unreviewed.length} of {postings.length} postings are marked reviewed. A posting counts only after you confirm its extraction is complete.</p>
        {unreviewed.length ? <>
          <label className="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" data-demo-id="review-all-ack" checked={ack} onChange={(e) => setAck(e.target.checked)} />I have checked the quotations for these {unreviewed.length} postings, or deliberately skipped what the course does not need.</label>
          <Button data-demo-id="review-all" disabled={!ack} onClick={() => { setSourcesReviewed(subject.id, unreviewed.map((s) => s.id), true); setAck(false); }}>Mark {unreviewed.length} postings reviewed</Button>
        </> : <p className="muted">All postings are reviewed. Unmark one from its card below if you need to revisit it.</p>}
      </div> : null}
    </> : null}
  </section>;
}

export function MeetingBriefPanel({ state, person, subject, mayEdit }: Props) {
  const [recommendation, setRecommendation] = useState<BriefRecommendation>("undecided");
  const [notes, setNotes] = useState("");
  const [recipients, setRecipients] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const briefs = state.evidenceBriefs.filter((b) => b.subjectId === subject.id).reverse();
  const current = briefs.find((b) => b.id === state.selectedBriefId) ?? briefs[0];
  const others = state.people.filter((p) => p.id !== person.id);
  const name = (id: string) => state.people.find((p) => p.id === id)?.name ?? id;
  useUnsavedEditor(Boolean(notes.trim()));
  return <section className="workspace-panel" aria-labelledby="meeting-brief" data-demo-id="meeting-brief">
    <div className="section-heading"><div><h3 id="meeting-brief">Meeting brief</h3><p className="muted">Turn the evidence into a document you can bring to a programme meeting, or send it to a colleague in Lyceum.</p></div></div>
    {mayEdit ? <>
      <div className="form-grid"><Field label="Your recommendation"><Select data-demo-id="brief-recommendation" value={recommendation} onChange={(e) => setRecommendation(e.target.value as BriefRecommendation)}>{(Object.keys(RECOMMENDATION_LABEL) as BriefRecommendation[]).map((r) => <option key={r} value={r}>{RECOMMENDATION_LABEL[r]}</option>)}</Select></Field></div>
      <Field label="Notes for the meeting" hint="What you propose, what it costs in hours, and what you want decided."><Textarea data-demo-id="brief-notes" value={notes} onChange={(e) => setNotes(e.target.value)} /></Field>
      <div className="button-row"><Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="brief-prepare" onClick={() => {
        const result = prepareEvidenceBrief(subject.id, { recommendation, notes });
        setMessage(result.ok ? "Brief prepared from the current evidence. Review it, then download or send it." : result.error);
        if (result.ok) setNotes("");
      }}>Prepare brief</Button></div>
      {message ? <p role="status" className="save-status">{message}</p> : null}
    </> : null}
    {current ? <article className="curriculum-object" data-demo-id="brief-current">
      <div className="section-heading"><div><h4>{RECOMMENDATION_LABEL[current.recommendation]}</h4>
        <p className="muted">Prepared {current.createdAt} by {name(current.createdBy)}{current.sentAt ? " · sent " + current.sentAt + " to " + current.recipients.map(name).join(", ") : " · not sent"}</p></div>
        <div className="button-row">
          <Button data-demo-id="brief-download" onClick={() => downloadText(subject.id + "-meeting-brief.md", current.markdown)}>Download brief (.md)</Button>
          <Button data-demo-id="brief-slides" onClick={() => { const outcomes = state.clos.filter((c) => c.subjectId === subject.id); void downloadDeck(briefDeck(subject, current, evidenceReport(subject.id, state.evidenceSources, state.skillMentions, state.skillMappings, outcomes), state.evidenceSources, state.skillMentions, outcomes, state.people, nowIso())); }}>Download slides (.pptx)</Button>
          {briefs.length > 1 ? <Select aria-label="Choose a prepared brief" value={current.id} onChange={(e) => selectBrief(e.target.value)}>{briefs.map((b) => <option key={b.id} value={b.id}>{b.createdAt} · {RECOMMENDATION_LABEL[b.recommendation]}</option>)}</Select> : null}
        </div></div>
      {current.notes ? <p className="preserve-lines">{current.notes}</p> : null}
      <p className="muted">The slide deck is generated from the current evidence and this brief's recommendation: decision, evidence base, table, coverage, options, limitations and one receipt slide per source. Editable in PowerPoint; no AI-written text.</p>
      <details><summary>Read the full brief</summary><pre className="brief-body">{current.markdown}</pre></details>
      {mayEdit && !current.sentAt ? <fieldset className="clo-choices"><legend>Send to</legend>
        {others.map((p) => <label key={p.id}><input type="checkbox" data-demo-id={"brief-recipient-" + p.id} checked={recipients.includes(p.id)} onChange={(e) => setRecipients(e.target.checked ? [...recipients, p.id] : recipients.filter((id) => id !== p.id))} /><span>{p.name} · {p.orgRole}</span></label>)}
        <div className="button-row"><Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="brief-send" disabled={!recipients.length} onClick={() => {
          const result = sendEvidenceBrief(current.id, recipients);
          setMessage(result.ok ? "Brief sent. Recipients see it on their Home page with the receipts attached." : result.error);
          if (result.ok) setRecipients([]);
        }}>Send brief</Button></div>
        <p className="muted">Sending notifies colleagues inside this local prototype. It is not an institutional submission.</p>
      </fieldset> : null}
    </article> : <p className="muted">No brief prepared yet. Record evidence above, then prepare one.</p>}
  </section>;
}

 succeeded in 236ms:
// The Course Studio (spec 6.3 / 6.4): the centrepiece. Subject editing, the
// review chain, and the assessment studio, kept calm with three quiet tabs so
// density stays opt-in. Works for every role that can reach it: the status and
// the person's hats decide which single primary action is on offer.

import { useState } from "react";
import { can, hatsOn, subjectsForPerson } from "../../app/roles.ts";
import {
  approveTestDraft,
  acknowledgeAssessmentCourseChange,
  resetAssessmentOutcomeWeights,
  canRunTest,
  createTestDraft,
  currentPerson,
  draftWithAgent,
  editCloChangeText,
  editDraftField,
  generateTestItems,
  navigate,
  personById,
  personWithHat,
  removeTestItem,
  requestAgentReview,
  reviewApprove,
  reviewRequestChanges,
  setCritique,
  selectSubject,
  selectStudioTab,
  startAcceptanceRun,
  startDraft,
  submitForReview,
  submitTestDraft,
  testDraftById,
  updateBlueprint,
  updateTestItem,
  useStore,
  type AppState,
} from "../../app/store.ts";
import type {
  BloomLevel,
  ChangeProposal,
  Person,
  ProposalEvent,
  ProposalStatus,
  Subject,
  TestDraft,
} from "../../types.ts";
import { AgentStrip } from "../shell/AgentStrip.tsx";
import { CurriculumPanel, CurriculumHistoryPanel } from "./CurriculumWorkspace.tsx";
import { EvidencePanel } from "./EvidenceWorkspace.tsx";
import { CourseOverview, TeachingPlanPanel } from "./CourseWorkspace.tsx";
import {
  Button,
  Card,
  EmptyState,
  Field,
  Input,
  Page,
  PageHead,
  Row,
  SectionLabel,
  Select,
  Tag,
  Textarea,
} from "../primitives/index.tsx";

const STATUS_LABEL: Record<ProposalStatus, string> = {
  drafting: "Drafting",
  "coordinator-review": "Coordinator review",
  testing: "Ready to test",
  "management-approval": "Awaiting management",
  approved: "Approved",
  rejected: "Rejected",
};

const STATUS_TONE: Record<ProposalStatus, "neutral" | "accent" | "ok" | "warn" | "danger"> = {
  drafting: "neutral",
  "coordinator-review": "warn",
  testing: "accent",
  "management-approval": "accent",
  approved: "ok",
  rejected: "danger",
};

const ACTION_LABEL: Record<ProposalEvent["action"], string> = {
  drafted: "Draft started",
  "agent-drafted": "Agent drafted",
  "agent-reviewed": "Agent reviewed",
  "submitted-for-review": "Submitted for review",
  "review-approved": "Review approved",
  "review-changes-requested": "Changes requested",
  tested: "Acceptance test run",
  approved: "Approved",
  rejected: "Rejected",
};

function fmtWhen(iso: string): string {
  const d = new Date(iso);
  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return iso;
  return d.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric" });
}

type TabId = AppState["studioTab"];
const STUDIO_TABS: { id: TabId; label: string }[] = [
  { id: "overview", label: "Overview" }, { id: "curriculum", label: "Outcomes & topics" }, { id: "evidence", label: "Evidence" }, { id: "plan", label: "Teaching plan" },
  { id: "content", label: "Proposal" }, { id: "assessment", label: "Assessment" },
  { id: "history", label: "History" },
];

export function StudioScreen() {
  const state = useStore();
  const person = currentPerson();
  if (!person) return null;
  const ownIds = subjectsForPerson(person.id, state.assignments);
  const subjects = state.subjects.filter((s) => person.orgRole !== "academic" || ownIds.includes(s.id));
  const subject = subjects.find((s) => s.id === state.selectedSubjectId) ?? subjects[0];
  if (!subject) return <Page><PageHead title="Course Studio" context="Your teaching workspace starts with an assigned course." /><EmptyState title="No course assigned yet" body="The department can assign you as a lecturer or coordinator in Assignments. Then your course outcomes, teaching plan and review workspace will appear here." action={<Button onClick={() => navigate("guide")}>Read the section guide</Button>} /></Page>;
  return <StudioCourse key={subject.id + person.id} state={state} person={person} subject={subject} subjects={subjects} />;
}

function StudioCourse({ state, person, subject, subjects }: { state: AppState; person: Person; subject: Subject; subjects: Subject[] }) {
  const tab = state.studioTab;
  const proposal = state.proposals.find((p) => p.subjectId === subject.id && p.status !== "approved" && p.status !== "rejected");
  const lastProposal = [...state.proposals].reverse().find((p) => p.subjectId === subject.id);
  const coordinator = personWithHat(subject.id, "coordinator");
  const mayDraft = can(person, "draft-change", { subjectId: subject.id, assignments: state.assignments });
  return <Page wide>
    <PageHead title={subject.id + " " + subject.title} context={<span>Year {subject.year} · Semester {subject.semester} · Coordinator: {coordinator?.name ?? "unassigned"}</span>} actions={
      <label className="course-switcher">Course<Select aria-label="Choose course" value={subject.id} onChange={(e) => selectSubject(e.target.value)}>{subjects.map((s) => <option key={s.id} value={s.id}>{s.id} · {s.title}</option>)}</Select></label>
    } />
    <div className="course-workspace-meta"><Tag>{subject.workspaceOnly ? "Personal course workspace" : subject.status === "proposed" ? "Proposed course" : "Course workspace"}</Tag><span role="status">{state.persistenceStatus === "unavailable" ? "Browser storage unavailable. Export your plan before closing." : state.persistenceStatus === "pending" ? "Saving in this browser…" : "Changes stored in this browser"}</span></div>
    <div className="studio-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Course workspace">
      {STUDIO_TABS.map((item, index) => <button key={item.id} role="tab" id={"studio-tab-" + item.id} aria-controls={"studio-panel-" + item.id} aria-selected={tab === item.id} tabIndex={tab === item.id ? 0 : -1} data-demo-id={"tab-" + item.id} onClick={() => selectStudioTab(item.id)} onKeyDown={(event) => {
        const keys = ["ArrowRight", "ArrowLeft", "Home", "End"];
        if (!keys.includes(event.key)) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        const next = event.key === "Home" ? 0 : event.key === "End" ? STUDIO_TABS.length - 1 : (index + (event.key === "ArrowRight" ? 1 : -1) + STUDIO_TABS.length) % STUDIO_TABS.length;
        selectStudioTab(STUDIO_TABS[next].id);
        document.getElementById("studio-tab-" + STUDIO_TABS[next].id)?.focus();
      }}>{item.label}</button>)}
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-overview" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-overview" hidden={tab !== "overview"} tabIndex={0}>
      <CourseOverview state={state} person={person} subject={subject} proposal={proposal} onCurriculum={() => selectStudioTab("curriculum")} onEvidence={() => selectStudioTab("evidence")} onPlan={() => selectStudioTab("plan")} onProposal={() => selectStudioTab("content")} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-curriculum" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-curriculum" hidden={tab !== "curriculum"} tabIndex={0}>
      <CurriculumPanel state={state} person={person} subject={subject} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-evidence" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-evidence" hidden={tab !== "evidence"} tabIndex={0}>
      <EvidencePanel state={state} person={person} subject={subject} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-plan" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-plan" hidden={tab !== "plan"} tabIndex={0}>
      <TeachingPlanPanel state={state} person={person} subject={subject} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-content" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-content" hidden={tab !== "content"} tabIndex={0}>
      {proposal ? <><div className="section-heading"><h2>Curriculum change proposal</h2><Tag tone={STATUS_TONE[proposal.status]}>{STATUS_LABEL[proposal.status]}</Tag></div><ContentTab key={proposal.id} state={state} person={person} subject={subject} proposal={proposal} /></> : <section className="workspace-panel"><h2>Plan a formal curriculum change</h2><p>A proposal holds the topic and outcome changes you want the coordinator and management to review. Your teaching plan can be prepared independently.</p>{lastProposal ? <p className="limitation">The previous proposal is {lastProposal.status}. Legacy proposal approval is a separate prototype workflow. Use Outcomes & topics for a lecturer-controlled course revision.</p> : null}{subject.workspaceOnly ? <Button variant="primary" onClick={() => selectStudioTab("curriculum")}>Open Outcomes & topics</Button> : mayDraft ? <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="studio-start-draft" onClick={() => startDraft(subject.id)}>Start a draft</Button> : <p className="muted">Only an assigned lecturer or coordinator can draft a change.</p>}</section>}
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-assessment" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-assessment" hidden={tab !== "assessment"} tabIndex={0}>
      <AssessmentTab state={state} person={person} subject={subject} proposal={proposal} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-history" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-history" hidden={tab !== "history"} tabIndex={0}>
      <CurriculumHistoryPanel state={state} subject={subject} />
      {lastProposal ? <HistoryTab state={state} subject={subject} proposal={proposal ?? lastProposal} /> : <section className="workspace-panel"><h2>Course history</h2><p>No proposal events are recorded yet. Starting a proposal creates its first event; teaching-session edits are saved separately in your plan.</p><p className="muted">Current version: {subject.currentVersionId}</p></section>}
    </div>
  </Page>;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Content: the draft, editable in place, with the agent modes, the critique,
// and the one status-driven primary action.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

function ContentTab(props: {
  state: AppState;
  person: Person;
  subject: Subject;
  proposal: ChangeProposal;
}) {
  const { state, person, subject, proposal } = props;
  const [mode, setMode] = useState<"self" | "agent" | "hybrid">("self");
  const [changesOpen, setChangesOpen] = useState(false);
  const [changeNote, setChangeNote] = useState("");

  const hats = hatsOn(person.id, subject.id, state.assignments);
  const coordHere = hats.includes("coordinator");
  const isAuthor = proposal.authorId === person.id;
  const mayReview =
    proposal.status === "coordinator-review" &&
    can(person, "review-draft", { subjectId: subject.id, assignments: state.assignments });

  // The topics textarea is uncontrolled (the store normalises lines, which would
  // eat newlines mid-typing); it remounts whenever the agent rewrites the draft.
  const agentDraftCount = proposal.history.filter((h) => h.action === "agent-drafted").length;
  const topicsKey = `${proposal.id}-topics-${agentDraftCount}`;

  const draft = proposal.draft;

  function pickMode(next: "self" | "agent" | "hybrid") {
    setMode(next);
    if (next === "agent" || next === "hybrid") draftWithAgent(proposal.id, next);
  }

  const modeButton = (id: "self" | "agent" | "hybrid", label: string) => (
    <Button
      variant="outline"
      data-demo-id={`mode-${id}`}
      onClick={() => pickMode(id)}
      style={{
        height: 30,
        padding: "0 12px",
        fontSize: 13,
        ...(mode === id
          ? {
              borderColor: "var(--accent)",
              color: "var(--accent)",
              background: "var(--accent-soft)",
            }
          : {}),
      }}
    >
      {label}
    </Button>
  );

  return (
    <div>
      <AgentStrip
        agent="authoring"
        idleText="Authoring drafts, reviews, and fixes. Pick a mode or ask for a review."
      />

      {mayReview ? (
        <Card focal style={{ marginBottom: 20 }}>
          <div style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 15, marginBottom: 4 }}>
            A lecturer's draft awaits your review
          </div>
          <p style={{ margin: "0 0 14px", fontSize: 13.5, color: "var(--ink-2)", maxWidth: 560 }}>
            Approve it for testing, or send it back with a note. Nothing reaches the acceptance
            test without your review.
          </p>
          <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 10 }}>
            <Button
              variant="primary"
              data-demo-id="review-approve"
              onClick={() => reviewApprove(proposal.id)}
            >
              Approve for testing
            </Button>
            <Button
              variant="quiet"
              data-demo-id="review-changes"
              onClick={() => setChangesOpen((v) => !v)}
            >
              Request changes
            </Button>
          </div>
          {changesOpen ? (
            <div style={{ marginTop: 12 }}>
              <Textarea
                value={changeNote}
                onChange={(e) => setChangeNote(e.target.value)}
                placeholder="What should change before this is tested?"
                style={{ minHeight: 64 }}
              />
              <Button
                variant="outline"
                style={{ marginTop: 8 }}
                onClick={() => {
                  reviewRequestChanges(proposal.id, changeNote.trim());
                  setChangesOpen(false);
                  setChangeNote("");
                }}
              >
                Send back to the author
              </Button>
            </div>
          ) : null}
        </Card>
      ) : null}

      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Drafting mode</SectionLabel>
      <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, marginBottom: 18 }}>
        {modeButton("self", "Self")}
        {modeButton("agent", "Agent drafts")}
        {modeButton("hybrid", "Hybrid")}
      </div>

      <Field label="Topics" hint="One topic per line.">
        <Textarea
          key={topicsKey}
          defaultValue={(draft.topics ?? []).join("\n")}
          onChange={(e) => editDraftField(proposal.id, "topics", e.target.value)}
          style={{ minHeight: 104 }}
        />
      </Field>

      <SectionLabel>Outcome changes</SectionLabel>
      {(draft.cloChanges ?? []).length === 0 ? (
        <EmptyState
          title="No outcome changes yet"
          body="Agent or hybrid mode drafts an edit to this subject's outcomes; you can refine every line."
        />
      ) : (
        (draft.cloChanges ?? []).map((c, i) => (
          <div
            key={`${c.cloId ?? "new"}-${i}`}
            style={{
              border: "1px solid var(--border)",
              borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
              padding: 12,
              marginBottom: 10,
              background: "var(--surface)",
            }}
          >
            <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 6, marginBottom: 8 }}>
              <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12.5, fontWeight: 600, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
                {c.cloId ?? "new outcome"}
              </span>
              <Tag tone={c.op === "remove" ? "danger" : c.op === "add" ? "ok" : "accent"}>{c.op}</Tag>
              <Tag>{c.bloomLevel}</Tag>
            </div>
            <Textarea
              data-demo-id={i === 0 ? "studio-draft-clo-0" : undefined}
              value={c.text}
              onChange={(e) => editCloChangeText(proposal.id, i, e.target.value)}
              style={{ minHeight: 64 }}
            />
          </div>
        ))
      )}

      <Field label="Test notes">
        <Textarea
          value={draft.testDraft ?? ""}
          onChange={(e) => editDraftField(proposal.id, "testDraft", e.target.value)}
          style={{ minHeight: 72 }}
        />
      </Field>
      <Field label="Lab notes">
        <Textarea
          value={draft.labDraft ?? ""}
          onChange={(e) => editDraftField(proposal.id, "labDraft", e.target.value)}
          style={{ minHeight: 72 }}
        />
      </Field>

      <div style={{ margin: "4px 0 16px" }}>
        <Button variant="quiet" onClick={() => requestAgentReview(proposal.id)}>
          Ask the agent to review
        </Button>
      </div>

      {state.critique ? (
        <div
          style={{
            background: "var(--warn-soft)",
            borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
            padding: "10px 12px",
            marginBottom: 18,
          }}
        >
          <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", justifyContent: "space-between" }}>
            <span style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13, color: "var(--warn)" }}>
              The agent's review
            </span>
            <Button
              variant="quiet"
              style={{ height: 24, padding: "0 8px", fontSize: 12 }}
              onClick={() => setCritique(null)}
            >
              Dismiss
            </Button>
          </div>
          <ul style={{ margin: "6px 0 0", paddingLeft: 18 }}>
            {state.critique.map((line, i) => (
              <li key={i} style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)", marginBottom: 2 }}>
                {line}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ) : null}

      {/* The one status-driven primary action. */}
      {isAuthor && !coordHere && proposal.status === "drafting" ? (
        <Button
          variant="primary"
          data-demo-id="studio-submit-review"
          onClick={() => submitForReview(proposal.id)}
        >
          Submit for coordinator review
        </Button>
      ) : canRunTest(proposal.id) ? (
        <Button
          variant="primary"
          data-demo-id="studio-run-test"
          onClick={() => startAcceptanceRun(proposal.id)}
        >
          Run the acceptance test
        </Button>
      ) : null}

      {proposal.status === "management-approval" ? (
        <div style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
          Tested. Awaiting management.{" "}
          <a
            href="#"
            onClick={(e) => {
              e.preventDefault();
              navigate("acceptance");
            }}
          >
            View the acceptance run
          </a>
        </div>
      ) : null}
      {proposal.status === "approved" ? (
        <div style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ok)" }}>
          Live. The prediction is recorded.{" "}
          <a
            href="#"
            onClick={(e) => {
              e.preventDefault();
              navigate("backtest");
            }}
          >
            See the closed loop
          </a>
        </div>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Assessment: the blueprint, agent-drafted items, the coverage meter, and the
// same review chain as the proposal (spec 6.4).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

const MIX_LEVELS: BloomLevel[] = ["Understand", "Apply", "Analyse"];

function AssessmentTab(props: {
  state: AppState;
  person: Person;
  subject: Subject;
  proposal?: ChangeProposal;
}) {
  const { state, person, subject, proposal } = props;
  const [selectedId,setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null);
  const tests = state.testDrafts.filter(t => t.subjectId === subject.id);
  const td = tests.find(t => t.id === selectedId) ?? testDraftById(proposal?.draft.testDraftId) ?? tests.at(-1);

  if (!td) {
    return (
      <EmptyState
        title="No test draft yet"
        body="Prepare a blueprint for this course. Local templates can draft example questions; review every task and mark allocation before using them. An assessment can be prepared without a curriculum proposal."
        action={
          <Button
            variant="primary"
            data-demo-id="assessment-start"
            onClick={() => createTestDraft(subject.id, proposal?.id)}
          >
            Start a test draft
          </Button>
        }
      />
    );
  }

  const weightSum = td.blueprint.cloWeights.reduce((s, w) => s + w.weight, 0);
  const mixSum = Object.values(td.blueprint.bloomMix).reduce<number>((s, v) => s + (v ?? 0), 0);
  const weightsOk = Math.abs(weightSum - 1) <= 0.01;
  const mixOk = mixSum <= 1;
  const hasItems = td.items.length > 0;

  return (
    <div>
      <Field label="Assessment draft"><Select value={td.id} onChange={e => setSelectedId(e.target.value)}>{tests.map(t => <option key={t.id} value={t.id}>{t.id} · {t.needsReview ? "Review course change" : t.status}</option>)}</Select></Field>
      <p className="limitation">Question generation uses local wording templates. It does not establish assessment quality; exact mark-allocation and task/rubric generation remain under development.</p>

      {td.needsReview ? <section className="workspace-panel">
        <h3>Review course change</h3>
        <p className="limitation">The course changed. Your questions are preserved; review their wording, outcome links, weights and marks before submitting again.</p>
        <Button onClick={() => resetAssessmentOutcomeWeights(td.id)}>Reset weights to current outcomes</Button>
        <p className="muted">This replaces the outcome weights with equal weights and keeps your questions. Remove questions linked to retired outcomes or draft new items, then adjust the weights.</p>
      </section> : null}

      {/* (a) the blueprint, editable */}
      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Blueprint</SectionLabel>
      <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginBottom: 12 }}>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, width: 130, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>Total marks</span>
        <Input
          type="number"
          min={1}
          className="num"
          style={{ width: 90 }}
          aria-label="Total assessment marks"
          value={td.blueprint.totalMarks}
          onChange={(e) =>
            updateBlueprint(td.id, { ...td.blueprint, totalMarks: Number(e.target.value) })
          }
        />
      </div>
      {td.blueprint.cloWeights.map((cw) => {
        const clo = state.clos.find((c) => c.id === cw.cloId);
        return (
          <div
            key={cw.cloId}
            style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginBottom: 8 }}
          >
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 13, width: 130, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              {cw.cloId} weight
            </span>
            <Input
              type="number"
              min={0}
              max={1}
              step={0.05}
              className="num"
              style={{ width: 90 }}
              aria-label={(clo?.label ?? cw.cloId) + " weight"}
              value={cw.weight}
              onChange={(e) =>
                updateBlueprint(td.id, {
                  ...td.blueprint,
                  cloWeights: td.blueprint.cloWeights.map((w) =>
                    w.cloId === cw.cloId ? { ...w, weight: Number(e.target.value) } : w,
                  ),
                })
              }
            />
            <span style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>{clo?.text ?? cw.cloId}</span>
          </div>
        );
      })}
      <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginTop: 12 }}>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, width: 130, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>Bloom mix</span>
        {MIX_LEVELS.map((level) => (
          <span key={level} style={{ display: "inline-flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 6 }}>
            <Input
              type="number"
              min={0}
              max={1}
              step={0.05}
              className="num"
              style={{ width: 74 }}
              aria-label={level + " share"}
              value={td.blueprint.bloomMix[level] ?? 0}
              onChange={(e) =>
                updateBlueprint(td.id, {
                  ...td.blueprint,
                  bloomMix: { ...td.blueprint.bloomMix, [level]: Number(e.target.value) },
                })
              }
            />
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>{level}</span>
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 8, margin: "14px 0 20px" }}>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-3)" }}>Blueprint check</span>
        <Tag tone={weightsOk ? "ok" : "danger"}>
          <span className="num">weights {weightSum.toFixed(2)}</span>
        </Tag>
        <Tag tone={mixOk ? "ok" : "danger"}>
          <span className="num">bloom mix {mixSum.toFixed(2)}</span>
        </Tag>
      </div>

      {/* (b) generation + (c) the items */}
      {hasItems ? (
        <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginBottom: 14 }}>
          <SectionLabel style={{ margin: 0 }}>Items</SectionLabel>
          <span style={{ flex: 1 }} />
          <Button
            variant="outline"
            data-demo-id="assessment-generate"
            onClick={() => generateTestItems(td.id)}
          >
            Draft items against the blueprint
          </Button>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <EmptyState
          title="No items yet"
          body="Local templates draft example wording from current outcomes. Review the questions, coverage and marks; every item stays editable."
          action={
            <Button
              variant="primary"
              data-demo-id="assessment-generate"
              onClick={() => generateTestItems(td.id)}
            >
              Draft items against the blueprint
            </Button>
          }
        />
      )}

      {td.items.map((it, idx) => (
        <Card key={it.id} style={{ marginBottom: 10, boxShadow: "none" }}>
          <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 8, marginBottom: 8 }}>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13 }}>
              Q{idx + 1}
            </span>
            <Tag>{it.bloomLevel}</Tag>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              {it.targetCLO}
            </span>
            {it.source === "human" ? <Tag>edited</Tag> : null}
            <span style={{ flex: 1 }} />
            <Input
              type="number"
              min={1}
              className="num"
              style={{ width: 70 }}
              aria-label={"Question " + (idx + 1) + " marks"}
              value={it.marks}
              onChange={(e) => updateTestItem(td.id, it.id, { marks: Number(e.target.value) })}
            />
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-3)" }}>marks</span>
            <Button
              variant="quiet"
              style={{ height: 28, padding: "0 8px", fontSize: 12.5 }}
              aria-label={"Remove question " + (idx + 1)}
              onClick={() => removeTestItem(td.id, it.id)}
            >
              Remove
            </Button>
          </div>
          <Textarea
            aria-label={"Question " + (idx + 1) + " wording"}
            value={it.text}
            onChange={(e) => updateTestItem(td.id, it.id, { text: e.target.value })}
            style={{ minHeight: 56 }}
          />
        </Card>
      ))}

      {/* (d) coverage meter */}
      {hasItems ? <CoverageMeter draft={td} /> : null}

      {/* (e) status action: exactly one primary at a time. */}
      {hasItems ? (
        <div style={{ marginTop: 20 }}>
          <TestStatusAction state={state} person={person} subject={subject} draft={td} />
        </div>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}

function CoverageMeter(props: { draft: TestDraft }) {
  const td = props.draft;
  const totalMarks = td.items.reduce((s, it) => s + it.marks, 0);
  const itemLevels = [...new Set<BloomLevel>([...MIX_LEVELS, ...td.items.map((it) => it.bloomLevel)])];

  const bar = (value: number, color: string) => (
    <div
      style={{
        height: 4,
        background: "var(--surface-2)",
        borderRadius: 2,
        marginTop: 3,
        maxWidth: 360,
      }}
    >
      <div
        style={{
          width: `${Math.min(100, Math.max(0, value * 100)).toFixed(1)}%`,
          height: "100%",
          background: color,
          borderRadius: 2,
        }}
      />
    </div>
  );

  return (
    <div style={{ marginTop: 20 }}>
      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Coverage against the blueprint</SectionLabel>
      {td.blueprint.cloWeights.map((cw) => {
        const actual =
          totalMarks > 0
            ? td.items.filter((it) => it.targetCLO === cw.cloId).reduce((s, it) => s + it.marks, 0) /
              totalMarks
            : 0;
        return (
          <div key={cw.cloId} style={{ marginBottom: 10 }}>
            <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              <span className="num" style={{ width: 48, fontWeight: 600 }}>
                {cw.cloId}
              </span>
              <span className="num">
                {(actual * 100).toFixed(0)}% of marks, planned {(cw.weight * 100).toFixed(0)}%
              </span>
            </div>
            {bar(actual, "var(--accent)")}

          </div>
        );
      })}
      {itemLevels.map((level) => {
        const share =
          td.items.length > 0
            ? td.items.filter((it) => it.bloomLevel === level).length / td.items.length
            : 0;
        const target = td.blueprint.bloomMix[level] ?? 0;
        return (
          <div key={level} style={{ marginBottom: 10 }}>
            <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              <span style={{ width: 90 }}>{level}</span>
              <span className="num">
                {(share * 100).toFixed(0)}% of items, mix {(target * 100).toFixed(0)}%
              </span>
            </div>
            {bar(share, "var(--accent)")}
            {bar(target, "var(--border)")}
          </div>
        );
      })}
    </div>
  );
}

function TestStatusAction(props: {
  state: AppState;
  person: Person;
  subject: Subject;
  draft: TestDraft;
}) {
  const { state, person, subject, draft } = props;

  const [reviewed,setReviewed] = useState(false);
  const [reviewError,setReviewError] = useState("");
  if (draft.needsReview) return <div>
    <label className="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" data-demo-id="assessment-course-change-ack" checked={reviewed} onChange={e => setReviewed(e.target.checked)} />I reviewed the blueprint and every question against the current course outcomes.</label>
    <Button data-demo-id="assessment-course-change-review" disabled={!reviewed} onClick={() => {
      const result = acknowledgeAssessmentCourseChange(draft.id,reviewed);
      setReviewError(result.ok ? "" : result.error ?? "The review could not be recorded.");
    }}>Record course-change review</Button>
    {reviewError ? <p role="alert" className="form-error">{reviewError}</p> : null}
  </div>;

  if (draft.status === "approved") {
    return (
      <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 8 }}>
        <Tag tone="ok">Approved</Tag>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
          {draft.proposalId ? "This local test decision is attached to the proposal." : "Local assessment decision recorded. Institutional approval remains in your university process."}
        </span>
      </div>
    );
  }

  if (
    draft.status === "coordinator-review" &&
    can(person, "review-draft", { subjectId: subject.id, assignments: state.assignments })
  ) {
    return (
      <Button variant="primary" onClick={() => approveTestDraft(draft.id)}>
        Approve test
      </Button>
    );
  }

  if (draft.status === "coordinator-review") {
    return (
      <span style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
        Sent for review. Awaiting the coordinator.
      </span>
    );
  }

  // Drafting: the author moves it on. A coordinator's own draft approves
  // directly; a lecturer's goes to the coordinator (both via submitTestDraft).
  if (draft.status === "drafting" && draft.authorId === person.id) {
    const authorIsCoordHere = hatsOn(draft.authorId, subject.id, state.assignments).includes(
      "coordinator",
    );
    return (
      <Button
        variant="primary"
        data-demo-id="assessment-submit"
        onClick={() => submitTestDraft(draft.id)}
      >
        {authorIsCoordHere ? "Approve test" : "Send test for review"}
      </Button>
    );
  }

  return null;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// History: the proposal's events, newest first, then the subject's versions.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HistoryTab(props: { state: AppState; subject: Subject; proposal: ChangeProposal }) {
  const { state, subject, proposal } = props;
  const events = [...proposal.history].reverse();
  const versions = [...state.subjectVersions]
    .filter((v) => v.subjectId === subject.id)
    .reverse();

  return (
    <div>
      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Proposal history</SectionLabel>
      {events.length === 0 ? (
        <EmptyState
          title="Nothing has happened yet"
          body="Proposal actions are recorded here. Course revision decisions appear above."
        />
      ) : (
        events.map((e, i) => (
          <Row key={`${e.at}-${e.action}-${i}`}>
            <span style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13, width: 180, flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {ACTION_LABEL[e.action]}
            </span>
            <span
              style={{
                flex: 1,
                fontSize: 13,
                color: "var(--ink-2)",
                overflow: "hidden",
                textOverflow: "ellipsis",
                whiteSpace: "nowrap",
              }}
            >
              {e.note ?? ""}
            </span>
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {personById(e.byPersonId)?.name ?? e.byPersonId}
            </span>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12, color: "var(--ink-3)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {fmtWhen(e.at)}
            </span>
          </Row>
        ))
      )}

      <SectionLabel>Subject versions</SectionLabel>
      {versions.length === 0 ? (
        <EmptyState
          title="No versions yet"
          body="Each approved change snapshots the subject here, so every revision stays traceable."
        />
      ) : (
        versions.map((v) => (
          <Row key={v.id}>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13, width: 120, flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {v.id}
            </span>
            <span
              style={{
                flex: 1,
                fontSize: 13,
                color: "var(--ink-2)",
                overflow: "hidden",
                textOverflow: "ellipsis",
                whiteSpace: "nowrap",
              }}
            >
              {v.reason}
            </span>
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {personById(v.changedBy)?.name ?? v.changedBy}
            </span>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12, color: "var(--ink-3)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {fmtWhen(v.changedAt)}
            </span>
          </Row>
        ))
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
// The app shell (spec 6.1): persistent sidebar with the person's nav and their
// subjects (hat badges), topbar with breadcrumb, search (command palette),
// notification bell and account menu, the toast, and the right-side agent
// panel. This chrome is what makes Lyceum read as an app you live in rather
// than a deck of screens.

import type { ReactNode } from "react";
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";
import { Bell, Check, ChevronDown, LogOut, Menu, RotateCcw, Search, ShieldCheck } from "lucide-react";
import type { Screen } from "../../app/roles.ts";
import { hatsOn, navFor, subjectsForPerson } from "../../app/roles.ts";
import {
  currentPerson,
  dismissToast,
  logout,
  navigate,
  resetWorkspace,
  selectSubject,
  switchUser,
  unreadFor,
  useStore,
} from "../../app/store.ts";
import { NAV_META, screenLabel } from "./nav.ts";
import { CommandPalette } from "./CommandPalette.tsx";
import { AgentPanel } from "./AgentPanel.tsx";
import { Kbd } from "../primitives/index.tsx";
import { PrototypeNotice } from "../primitives/PrototypeNotice.tsx";
import { SectionHelp } from "../primitives/SectionHelp.tsx";

const SIDEBAR_W = 240;
const TOPBAR_H = 56;

export function Shell(props: { children: ReactNode }) {
  const state = useStore();
  const person = currentPerson();
  const [paletteOpen, setPaletteOpen] = useState(false);
  const [menuOpen, setMenuOpen] = useState(false);
  const [navOpen, setNavOpen] = useState(false);
  const mainRef = useRef<HTMLElement>(null);
  const menuRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

  // Cmd+K / Ctrl+K opens the palette from anywhere.
  useEffect(() => {
    function onKey(e: KeyboardEvent) {
      if ((e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) && e.key.toLowerCase() === "k") {
        e.preventDefault();
        setPaletteOpen((v) => !v);
      }
      if (e.key === "Escape") { setMenuOpen(false); setNavOpen(false); }
    }
    window.addEventListener("keydown", onKey);
    return () => window.removeEventListener("keydown", onKey);
  }, []);

  // Click-away for the account menu.
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!menuOpen) return;
    function onClick(e: MouseEvent) {
      if (menuRef.current && !menuRef.current.contains(e.target as Node)) setMenuOpen(false);
    }
    window.addEventListener("mousedown", onClick);
    return () => window.removeEventListener("mousedown", onClick);
  }, [menuOpen]);

  // Toast auto-dismiss.
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!state.toast) return;
    const t = setTimeout(() => dismissToast(), 4000);
    return () => clearTimeout(t);
  }, [state.toast]);

  useEffect(() => {
    setNavOpen(false);
    mainRef.current?.scrollTo(0, 0);
    mainRef.current?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    document.title = screenLabel(state.screen) + " · Lyceum";
  }, [state.screen, state.selectedSubjectId]);

  if (!person) return <>{props.children}</>;

  const nav = navFor(person, state.assignments);
  const mySubjects = subjectsForPerson(person.id, state.assignments);
  const unread = unreadFor(person.id).length;

  const roleLine =
    person.orgRole === "management"
      ? "Management"
      : person.orgRole === "department"
        ? "Department"
        : "Academic";

  return (
    <div className={"app-shell" + (navOpen ? " nav-open" : "")} style={{ display: "flex", height: "100%", overflow: "hidden" }}>
      <a className="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>
      <div className="mobile-navigation"><span className="page-title">Lyceum</span><button aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-expanded={navOpen} aria-controls="primary-sidebar" onClick={() => setNavOpen((open) => !open)}><Menu size={20} /> Navigation</button></div>
      {/* ---------- sidebar ---------- */}
      <aside
        id="primary-sidebar"
        className="app-sidebar"
        onClick={(event) => { if ((event.target as HTMLElement).closest("button")) setNavOpen(false); }}
        style={{
          width: SIDEBAR_W,
          flexShrink: 0,
          borderRight: "1px solid var(--border)",
          background: "var(--surface)",
          display: "flex",
          flexDirection: "column",
          overflowY: "auto",
        }}
      >
        <div style={{ padding: "18px 16px 10px" }}>
          <button
            className="page-title"
            style={{ fontSize: 21, cursor: "pointer", border: 0, padding: 0, background: "none", color: "var(--ink)" }}
            onClick={() => navigate("inbox")}
          >
            Lyceum
          </button>
          <div style={{ fontSize: 11.5, color: "var(--ink-3)", marginTop: 2 }}>
            Curriculum advisory
          </div>
        </div>

        <nav aria-label="Main navigation" style={{ padding: "6px 8px", flex: 1 }}>
          {nav
            .filter((s) => s !== "backtest" && s !== "office" && s !== "dataroom" && s !== "index" && s !== "guide")
            .map((s) => (
              <NavItem key={s} screen={s} active={state.screen === s} badge={s === "inbox" ? unread : 0} />
            ))}

          {mySubjects.length > 0 ? (
            <>
              <div
                style={{
                  fontSize: 11,
                  fontWeight: 600,
                  color: "var(--ink-3)",
                  letterSpacing: "0.03em",
                  padding: "16px 10px 4px",
                }}
              >
                MY SUBJECTS
              </div>
              {mySubjects.map((sid) => {
                const hats = hatsOn(person.id, sid, state.assignments);
                return (
                  <button
                    key={sid}
                    data-demo-id={`subject-${sid}`}
                    onClick={() => {
                      selectSubject(sid);
                      navigate("studio");
                    }}
                    style={{
                      width: "100%", border: "none", minHeight: 36,
                      display: "flex",
                      alignItems: "center",
                      justifyContent: "space-between",
                      padding: "6px 10px",
                      borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
                      cursor: "pointer",
                      color: "var(--ink-2)",
                      fontSize: 13,
                      background:
                        state.selectedSubjectId === sid && state.screen === "studio"
                          ? "var(--accent-soft)"
                          : "transparent",
                    }}
                  >
                    <span className="num">{sid}</span>
                    <span style={{ display: "flex", gap: 3 }}>
                      {hats.includes("coordinator") ? <HatBadge label="C" title="Coordinator" /> : null}
                      {hats.includes("lecturer") ? <HatBadge label="L" title="Lecturer" /> : null}
                    </span>
                  </button>
                );
              })}
            </>
          ) : null}

          <div
            style={{
              fontSize: 11,
              fontWeight: 600,
              color: "var(--ink-3)",
              letterSpacing: "0.03em",
              padding: "16px 10px 4px",
            }}
          >
            EVIDENCE
          </div>
          {(["backtest", "dataroom", "office", "index"] as Screen[])
            .filter((s) => nav.includes(s))
            .map((s) => (
              <NavItem key={s} screen={s} active={state.screen === s} badge={0} />
            ))}
          <div style={{ marginTop: 12, borderTop: "1px solid var(--border)", paddingTop: 8 }}><NavItem screen="guide" active={state.screen === "guide"} badge={0} /></div>
        </nav>

        <div style={{ padding: "10px 16px", borderTop: "1px solid var(--border)", fontSize: 11.5, color: "var(--ink-3)" }}>
          Illustrative survey-based scenarios.
          <br />
          Uncalibrated Rasch-style model.
        </div>
      </aside>

      {/* ---------- main column ---------- */}
      <div style={{ flex: 1, display: "flex", flexDirection: "column", minWidth: 0, minHeight: 0 }}>
        <header
          className="app-topbar"
          style={{
            height: TOPBAR_H,
            flexShrink: 0,
            display: "flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            gap: 12,
            padding: "0 20px",
            borderBottom: "1px solid var(--border)",
            background: "var(--surface)",
          }}
        >
          <div style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 15 }}>{screenLabel(state.screen)}</div>
          <div style={{ flex: 1 }} />

          <button
            className="search-trigger"
            onClick={() => setPaletteOpen(true)}
            aria-label="Search (Ctrl+K)"
            style={{
              display: "flex",
              alignItems: "center",
              gap: 8,
              height: 34,
              padding: "0 12px",
              borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
              border: "1px solid var(--border)",
              background: "var(--bg)",
              color: "var(--ink-3)",
              cursor: "pointer",
              fontSize: 13,
              minWidth: 200,
            }}
          >
            <Search size={15} />
            <span style={{ flex: 1, textAlign: "left" }}>Search or jump to</span>
            <Kbd>Ctrl K</Kbd>
          </button>

          <button
            data-demo-id="topbar-bell"
            onClick={() => navigate("inbox")}
            aria-label={`Notifications, ${unread} unread`}
            style={{
              position: "relative",
              display: "flex",
              alignItems: "center",
              justifyContent: "center",
              width: 36,
              height: 36,
              borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
              border: "1px solid var(--border)",
              background: "var(--surface)",
              cursor: "pointer",
              color: "var(--ink-2)",
            }}
          >
            <Bell size={17} />
            {unread > 0 ? (
              <span
                className="num"
                style={{
                  position: "absolute",
                  top: -5,
                  right: -5,
                  minWidth: 17,
                  height: 17,
                  padding: "0 4px",
                  borderRadius: 999,
                  background: "var(--accent)",
                  color: "var(--accent-ink)",
                  fontSize: 10.5,
                  fontWeight: 600,
                  display: "flex",
                  alignItems: "center",
                  justifyContent: "center",
                }}
              >
                {unread}
              </span>
            ) : null}
          </button>

          {/* account menu */}
          <div ref={menuRef} style={{ position: "relative" }}>
            <button
              className="account-trigger"
              aria-label={"Account: " + person.name}
              aria-expanded={menuOpen}
              aria-controls="account-options"
              data-demo-id="account-menu"
              onClick={() => setMenuOpen((v) => !v)}
              style={{
                display: "flex",
                alignItems: "center",
                gap: 8,
                height: 36,
                padding: "0 10px",
                borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
                border: "1px solid var(--border)",
                background: "var(--surface)",
                cursor: "pointer",
              }}
            >
              <Avatar name={person.name} />
              <span className="account-name" style={{ fontSize: 13, fontWeight: 500 }}>{person.name}</span>
              {person.verified ? (
                <ShieldCheck size={14} color="var(--ok)" aria-label="Verified" />
              ) : null}
              <ChevronDown size={14} color="var(--ink-3)" />
            </button>
            {menuOpen ? (
              <div
                id="account-options"
                className="fade-up"
                style={{
                  position: "absolute",
                  right: 0,
                  top: 42,
                  width: 260,
                  background: "var(--surface)",
                  border: "1px solid var(--border)",
                  borderRadius: "var(--radius-m)",
                  boxShadow: "var(--shadow-2)",
                  padding: 6,
                  zIndex: 60,
                }}
              >
                <div style={{ padding: "8px 10px", borderBottom: "1px solid var(--border)" }}>
                  <div style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13 }}>{person.name}</div>
                  <div style={{ fontSize: 12, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
                    {roleLine}
                    {person.email ? ` · ${person.email}` : ""}
                  </div>
                  <div style={{ fontSize: 11.5, marginTop: 3, color: person.verified ? "var(--ok)" : "var(--warn)" }}>
                    {person.verified
                      ? "Verified coordinator identity"
                      : "Unverified: edits carry an unverified tag"}
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div style={{ padding: "6px 10px 2px", fontSize: 11, fontWeight: 600, color: "var(--ink-3)" }}>
                  SWITCH PERSON
                </div>
                {state.people.map((p) => (
                  <button
                    key={p.id}
                    data-demo-id={`switch-${p.id}`}
                    onClick={() => {
                      switchUser(p.id);
                      setMenuOpen(false);
                    }}
                    style={menuItemStyle}
                  >
                    <Avatar name={p.name} />
                    <span style={{ flex: 1, textAlign: "left" }}>{p.name}</span>
                    {p.id === person.id ? <Check size={14} color="var(--accent)" /> : null}
                  </button>
                ))}
                <div style={{ borderTop: "1px solid var(--border)", marginTop: 4, paddingTop: 4 }}>
                  <button
                    onClick={() => {
                      if (window.confirm("Reset this browser's workspace? This removes saved teaching plans, drafts and uploads. Export any plan you want to keep first.")) resetWorkspace();
                      setMenuOpen(false);
                    }}
                    style={menuItemStyle}
                  >
                    <RotateCcw size={14} />
                    <span>Reset workspace</span>
                  </button>
                  <button
                    onClick={() => {
                      logout();
                      setMenuOpen(false);
                    }}
                    style={menuItemStyle}
                  >
                    <LogOut size={14} />
                    <span>Sign out</span>
                  </button>
                </div>
              </div>
            ) : null}
          </div>
        </header>

        <main ref={mainRef} id="main-content" tabIndex={-1} style={{ flex: 1, overflowY: "auto", minWidth: 0 }} data-demo-id="main-scroll">
          <PrototypeNotice />
          {state.persistenceStatus === "unavailable" ? <div role="alert" className="storage-warning">Browser storage is unavailable. Changes only last while this page is open. Export your teaching plan before closing.</div> : null}
          <SectionHelp screen={state.screen} />
          {props.children}
        </main>
      </div>

      {/* ---------- overlays ---------- */}
      {paletteOpen ? <CommandPalette onClose={() => setPaletteOpen(false)} /> : null}
      <AgentPanel />
      {state.toast ? (
        <div
          className="fade-up"
          role="status"
          aria-live="polite"
          style={{
            position: "fixed",
            bottom: 22,
            left: "50%",
            transform: "translateX(-50%)",
            background: "var(--ink)",
            color: "#fff",
            padding: "9px 16px",
            borderRadius: "var(--radius-m)",
            boxShadow: "var(--shadow-2)",
            fontSize: 13.5,
            zIndex: 80,
            maxWidth: 520,
          }}
        >
          {state.toast}
}

const menuItemStyle: React.CSSProperties = {
  display: "flex",
  alignItems: "center",
  gap: 8,
  width: "100%",
  padding: "7px 10px",
  border: "none",
  background: "transparent",
  borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
  cursor: "pointer",
  fontSize: 13,
  color: "var(--ink)",
};

function NavItem(props: { screen: Screen; active: boolean; badge: number }) {
  if (props.screen === "login") return null;
  const meta = NAV_META[props.screen];
  const Icon = meta.icon;
  return (
    <button
      data-demo-id={`nav-${props.screen}`}
      onClick={() => navigate(props.screen)}
      aria-current={props.active ? "page" : undefined}
      style={{
        display: "flex",
        alignItems: "center",
        gap: 10,
        width: "100%",
        padding: "7px 10px",
        marginBottom: 1,
        borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
        border: "none",
        cursor: "pointer",
        fontSize: 13.5,
        fontWeight: props.active ? 600 : 400,
        color: props.active ? "var(--accent)" : "var(--ink-2)",
        background: props.active ? "var(--accent-soft)" : "transparent",
        transition: "background 150ms ease-out",
      }}
    >
      <Icon size={16} strokeWidth={1.75} />
      <span style={{ flex: 1, textAlign: "left" }}>{meta.label}</span>
      {props.badge > 0 ? (
        <span
          className="num"
          style={{
            minWidth: 18,
            height: 18,
            padding: "0 5px",
            borderRadius: 999,
            background: "var(--accent)",
            color: "var(--accent-ink)",
            fontSize: 11,
            fontWeight: 600,
            display: "flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            justifyContent: "center",
          }}
        >
          {props.badge}
        </span>
      ) : null}
    </button>
  );
}

function HatBadge(props: { label: string; title: string }) {
  return (
    <span
      title={props.title}
      style={{
        width: 16,
        height: 16,
        borderRadius: 4,
        background: "var(--surface-2)",
        color: "var(--ink-3)",
        fontSize: 10,
        fontWeight: 600,
        display: "inline-flex",
        alignItems: "center",
        justifyContent: "center",
      }}
    >
      {props.label}
    </span>
  );
}

function Avatar(props: { name: string }) {
  const initials = props.name
    .split(" ")
    .map((w) => w[0])
    .slice(0, 2)
    .join("");
  return (
    <span
      aria-hidden
      style={{
        width: 24,
        height: 24,
        borderRadius: "50%",
        background: "var(--accent-soft)",
        color: "var(--accent)",
        fontSize: 10.5,
        fontWeight: 600,
        display: "inline-flex",
        alignItems: "center",
        justifyContent: "center",
        flexShrink: 0,
      }}
    >
      {initials}
    </span>
  );
}
/* Lyceum v3 global styles (spec Section 3). Plain surfaces, no decorative
   canvas. The product's character comes from spacing, hierarchy and motion. */

:root {
  --bg: #f7f7f5;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --surface-2: #f1f1ee;
  --ink: #191c1f;
  --ink-2: #55595e;
  --ink-3: #62676d;
  --accent: #3b5bdb;
  --accent-ink: #ffffff;
  --accent-soft: #edf0fc;
  --ok: #1f7a4d;
  --ok-soft: #e7f3ec;
  --warn: #925108;
  --warn-soft: #fcf0e0;
  --danger: #c0392b;
  --danger-soft: #fae9e7;
  --border: #e4e4e0;
  --control-border: #858990;
  --shadow-1: 0 1px 2px rgba(25, 28, 31, 0.06);
  --shadow-2: 0 4px 16px rgba(25, 28, 31, 0.1);
  --radius-s: 6px;
  --radius-m: 10px;
  --radius-l: 14px;
  --font-ui: "Inter", system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-display: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
}

* {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

html,
body,
#root {
  height: 100%;
}

body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-ui);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
}

/* Numbers align in tables and stat lines without a separate mono font. */
.num,
td.num,
.tabular {
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}

h1,
h2,
h3,
h4 {
  margin: 0;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.25;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}

/* Page titles carry the academic voice: the serif, and only here. */
.page-title {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 26px;
  letter-spacing: 0;
}

a {
  color: var(--accent);
  text-decoration: none;
}
a:hover {
  text-decoration: underline;
}

button {
  font-family: inherit;
}

input,
textarea,
select {
  font-family: inherit;
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--ink);
}

::placeholder {
  color: var(--ink-3);
}

/* Visible keyboard focus, everywhere. */
:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
  border-radius: 2px;
}

/* Scrollbars, quiet. */
* {
  scrollbar-width: thin;
  scrollbar-color: var(--border) transparent;
}

/* ---------- shared keyframes ---------- */

@keyframes fadeUp {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}

@keyframes fadeIn {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}

@keyframes shimmer {
  0% {
    background-position: -200px 0;
  }
  100% {
    background-position: 200px 0;
  }
}

@keyframes pulseDot {
  0%,
  100% {
    opacity: 0.35;
  }
  50% {
    opacity: 1;
  }
}

@keyframes spin {
  to {
    transform: rotate(360deg);
  }
}

.fade-up {
  animation: fadeUp 220ms ease-out both;
}
.fade-in {
  animation: fadeIn 180ms ease-out both;
}

/* The working shimmer for agent strips. */
.agent-shimmer {
  background: linear-gradient(
    90deg,
    var(--surface-2) 0%,
    var(--accent-soft) 50%,
    var(--surface-2) 100%
  );
  background-size: 200px 100%;
  animation: shimmer 1.4s linear infinite;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
  }
}

/* Course preparation and help share a small, responsive workspace vocabulary. */
.page-heading { flex-wrap: wrap; }
.page-content { width: 100%; }
.page-content h2 { font-size: 18px; }
.page-content h3 { font-size: 16px; }
.page-content h4 { font-size: 14px; }
.page-content p { margin: 10px 0 16px; }
.muted { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 13px; }
.eyebrow { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.button-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.section-heading { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0 0 16px; }
.section-heading > div { min-width: 0; }
.section-heading p { margin-bottom: 0; }
.workspace-panel { background: var(--surface); padding: 22px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-m); margin-bottom: 20px; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.workspace-panel > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.workspace-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.65fr) minmax(260px, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
.home-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(260px, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
.home-focus { border-top: 3px solid var(--accent); }
.home-focus h2 { font-size: 23px; }
.course-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
.course-grid > .workspace-panel { margin-bottom: 0; }
.course-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
.course-card > .section-heading { width: 100%; }
.course-card > button { margin-top: auto; }
.course-facts { width: 100%; margin: 0 0 18px; }
.course-facts > div { display: flex; gap: 12px; justify-content: space-between; padding: 7px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 13px; }
dt { font-weight: 600; }
.course-facts dd { margin: 0; text-align: right; color: var(--ink-2); }
.course-next { margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 13px; }
.course-next p { margin: 4px 0 0; }
.course-workspace-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12px; margin: -8px 0 16px; }
.course-switcher { display: grid; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); width: min(300px, 100%); }
.studio-tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 24px; overflow-x: auto; }
.studio-tabs > button { padding: 12px 16px; min-height: 44px; white-space: nowrap; border: 0; background: transparent; color: var(--ink-2); border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; font-size: 14px; cursor: pointer; }
.studio-tabs > button[aria-selected="true"] { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
.studio-tabs > button:focus-visible { outline-offset: -3px; }
.preparation-summary { display: flex; gap: 12px 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 16px 0; margin: 0 0 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 13px; }
.preparation-summary strong { font-size: 18px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--ink); margin-right: 4px; }
.outcome-list, .source-list, .work-list, .checklist { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.outcome-list li, .source-list li, .work-list li { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 14px 0; }
.outcome-list p { margin: 8px 0; }
.source-list strong, .source-list span, .work-list span { display: block; }
.source-list span, .work-list span { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: 3px; }
.work-list li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 14px; align-items: center; }
.checklist li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; margin: 16px 0; font-size: 13px; }
.checklist li > span:first-child { flex-shrink: 0; }
.context-list > div { margin: 12px 0; }
.context-list dt { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); }
.context-list dd { margin: 3px 0; }
.filter-bar { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; margin: 24px 0 0; }
.filter-bar > .form-field { flex: 1; min-width: 160px; margin-bottom: 0 !important; }
.course-filters > .form-field:first-child { flex: 2; }
.form-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
.clo-choices { border: 1px solid var(--control-border); border-radius: var(--radius-s); margin: 0 0 20px; padding: 8px 12px; }
.clo-choices legend { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; padding: 0 4px; }
.clo-choices label { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px; padding: 10px 0; cursor: pointer; }
.clo-choices input { width: 18px; height: 18px; flex-shrink: 0; margin: 2px 0; accent-color: var(--accent); }
.session-editor { border-color: var(--control-border); }
.inline-field { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 13px; }
.inline-field select { width: auto !important; }
.session-content { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; }
.session-actions { margin-top: 20px; }
.preserve-lines { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.form-error, .storage-warning { padding: 12px 16px; background: var(--danger-soft); color: var(--danger); border-radius: var(--radius-s); margin-bottom: 16px; }
.storage-warning { margin: 12px 32px; }
.save-status { color: var(--ok); }
.limitation { padding: 12px 14px; border-left: 3px solid var(--warn); background: var(--warn-soft); font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink); }
.section-help { margin: 10px 32px 0; max-width: 1256px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 13px; }
summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 10px 2px; min-height: 40px; }
.section-help > summary { width: fit-content; }
.section-help-body { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-s); padding: 12px 20px; }
.section-help ol, .guide-entry ol { padding-left: 22px; }
.section-help li, .guide-entry li { margin: 8px 0; }
.guide-entry { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-s); margin: 10px 0; }
.guide-entry > summary { padding: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
.guide-entry > summary > span:first-child { margin-right: 12px; }
.guide-entry-body { padding: 0 20px 20px; }
.journey-list { padding-left: 24px; }
.journey-list li { padding: 6px 0; }
.remaining-work { margin-top: 36px; }
.remaining-work dl > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 1fr) 3fr; gap: 20px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 18px 0; }
.remaining-work dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-2); }
.skip-link { position: fixed; top: 10px; left: 10px; transform: translateY(-150%); z-index: 200; background: var(--surface); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; padding: 10px 16px; }
.skip-link:focus { transform: none; }
.mobile-navigation { display: none; }
.app-sidebar nav button { min-height: 36px; }
[hidden] { display: none !important; }

@media (max-width: 1100px) {
  .workspace-columns, .home-columns { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0; }
  .course-aside { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }
  .course-aside .workspace-panel { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .course-aside .workspace-panel:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .search-trigger { min-width: 44px !important; }
  .search-trigger > span { display: none !important; }
}
@media (max-width: 760px) {
  .app-shell { flex-direction: column; }
  .mobile-navigation { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: var(--surface); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 6px 16px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .mobile-navigation > button { min-height: 44px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: var(--radius-s); color: var(--ink); }
  .app-sidebar { display: none !important; width: 100% !important; max-height: 45vh; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .nav-open .app-sidebar { display: flex !important; }
  .app-sidebar nav button { min-height: 44px; }
  .app-topbar { gap: 8px !important; padding: 0 16px !important; }
  .app-topbar button { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; }
  .account-name, .account-trigger > svg { display: none; }
  .page-content { padding: 20px 16px 44px !important; }
  .section-help { margin: 8px 16px 0; }
  .storage-warning { margin: 12px 16px; }
  .page-heading-actions { width: 100%; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .course-switcher { width: 100%; }
  .course-grid, .form-grid, .session-content, .course-aside { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .studio-tabs { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .studio-tabs > button { padding: 10px 12px; }
  .course-aside .workspace-panel:last-child { grid-column: auto; }
  .workspace-panel { padding: 18px; }
  .session-content { gap: 4px; }
  .filter-bar > .form-field { min-width: 100%; }
  .course-facts > div { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 12px; }
  .remaining-work dl > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  .guide-entry > summary > span { white-space: normal !important; }
  .page-content button { min-height: 44px; }
  .page-content input:not([type="checkbox"]), .page-content select { min-height: 44px; }
}

