// The lecturer's research run: fetch postings from a permitted board on request,
// keep the ones worth reading, scan them for the skills the lecturer names,
// confirm each exact quotation, vouch for the extraction, then turn the result
// into a meeting brief that can be downloaded or sent to a colleague.

import { useState } from "react";
import {
  clearCollection, clearProposals, confirmProposals, dismissProposal, importCollectedPostings, nowIso, prepareEvidenceBrief, runCollection,
  scanForRequirements, selectBrief, sendEvidenceBrief, setSkillLexicon, setSourcesReviewed, type AppState,
} from "../../app/store.ts";
import { briefDeck, downloadDeck } from "../../lib/slides.ts";
import { BOARD_TOKEN, SOURCE_POLICIES, matchedKeywords, parseKeywords } from "../../lib/collect.ts";
import { RECOMMENDATION_LABEL, REQUIREMENT_LEVELS, evidenceReport, parseLexicon, type MentionProposal } from "../../lib/evidence.ts";
import { downloadText } from "../../lib/download.ts";
import type { BriefRecommendation, CollectionProvider, MentionRequirement, Person, Subject } from "../../types.ts";
import { Button, Field, Input, Select, Tag, Textarea } from "../primitives/index.tsx";
import { useUnsavedEditor } from "../useUnsavedEditor.ts";

type Props = { state: AppState; person: Person; subject: Subject; mayEdit: boolean };
const PROVIDERS = Object.keys(SOURCE_POLICIES) as CollectionProvider[];

export function ResearchRun({ state, subject, mayEdit }: Props) {
  const [provider, setProvider] = useState<CollectionProvider>("sample");
  const [board, setBoard] = useState("");
  const [query, setQuery] = useState("");
  const [inText, setInText] = useState(false);
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const run = state.collectRun && state.collectRun.subjectId === subject.id ? state.collectRun : null;
  const policy = SOURCE_POLICIES[provider];
  const postings = run?.status === "done" ? run.postings : [];
  const keywords = parseKeywords(run?.query ?? "");
  const imported = new Set(state.evidenceSources.filter((s) => s.subjectId === subject.id).map((s) => s.collection?.postingId ?? ""));
  const boardOk = provider === "sample" || BOARD_TOKEN.test(board.trim());
  async function fetchNow() {
    setMessage(""); setSelected([]);
    const result = await runCollection(subject.id, { provider, board, query, inText });
    if (!result.ok) setMessage(result.error);
  }
  return <section className="workspace-panel" aria-labelledby="research-run">
    <div className="section-heading"><div><h3 id="research-run">Research run</h3><p className="muted">Fetch postings from a permitted employer board when you ask, then keep the ones worth reading as evidence.</p></div></div>
    {mayEdit ? <>
      <div className="form-grid">
        <Field label="Source"><Select data-demo-id="collect-provider" value={provider} onChange={(e) => { setProvider(e.target.value as CollectionProvider); setMessage(""); }}>{PROVIDERS.map((p) => <option key={p} value={p}>{SOURCE_POLICIES[p].name}</option>)}</Select></Field>
        {provider !== "sample" ? <Field label="Employer board token" hint={provider === "greenhouse" ? "The name in boards.greenhouse.io/NAME, or in an employer's careers link." : "The name in jobs.lever.co/NAME."}><Input data-demo-id="collect-board" maxLength={80} value={board} onChange={(e) => setBoard(e.target.value)} placeholder={provider === "greenhouse" ? "e.g. stripe" : "e.g. palantir"} /></Field> : null}
        <Field label="Role keywords" hint="Comma-separated. Matches posting titles; tick the box below to search inside the text too."><Input data-demo-id="collect-query" value={query} onChange={(e) => setQuery(e.target.value)} placeholder="e.g. data analyst, analytics" /></Field>
      </div>
      <label className="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" checked={inText} onChange={(e) => setInText(e.target.checked)} />Also match keywords inside the posting text</label>
      <details className="guide-entry"><summary><span>Source policy: {policy.name}</span><Tag tone={policy.enabled ? "ok" : "warn"}>{policy.enabled ? "Permitted on request" : "Disabled"}</Tag></summary>
        <div className="guide-entry-body"><dl className="context-list"><div><dt>Owner</dt><dd>{policy.owner}</dd></div><div><dt>Method</dt><dd>{policy.method}</dd></div><div><dt>Retention</dt><dd>{policy.retention}</dd></div><div><dt>Refresh</dt><dd>{policy.refresh}</dd></div><div><dt>Policy reviewed</dt><dd>{policy.policyReviewedOn}</dd></div></dl><p className="muted">{policy.note}</p></div></details>
      <div className="button-row">
        <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="collect-run" disabled={run?.status === "running" || !boardOk} onClick={() => void fetchNow()}>{run?.status === "running" ? "Fetching..." : "Fetch postings"}</Button>
        {run ? <Button onClick={() => { clearCollection(); setSelected([]); setMessage(""); }}>Clear results</Button> : null}
      </div>
      {message ? <p role="alert" className="form-error">{message}</p> : null}
      {run ? <div data-demo-id="collect-log"><div className="button-row"><h4>Collection log</h4>{run.status === "running" ? <Tag tone="warn">Fetching now</Tag> : run.status === "failed" ? <Tag tone="danger">Failed</Tag> : run.provider === "sample" ? <Tag>Saved sample, no network</Tag> : run.cached ? <Tag tone="accent">Local cache of a live fetch</Tag> : <Tag tone="ok">Fetched live</Tag>}</div>
        <ol className="collect-log" aria-live="polite">{run.log.map((line, i) => <li key={i}>{line}</li>)}</ol></div> : null}
      {run?.status === "failed" ? <p role="alert" className="form-error">{run.error}</p> : null}
      {run?.status === "done" ? <div>
        <p role="status" className="save-status" data-demo-id="collect-status">{postings.length} of {run.total} postings match{run.query ? " \"" + run.query + "\"" : ""} on {run.label}. Retrieved {run.retrievedAt}{run.cached ? ", served from the local cache" : ""}. Publication dates are shown as published; the retrieval time is kept separately.</p>
        {postings.length ? <>
          <div className="button-row">
            <Button data-demo-id="collect-select-all" onClick={() => setSelected(postings.filter((p) => !imported.has(p.id)).map((p) => p.id))}>Select all shown</Button>
            <Button onClick={() => setSelected([])}>Clear selection</Button>
            <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="collect-import" disabled={!selected.length} onClick={() => {
              const result = importCollectedPostings(subject.id, selected);
              setMessage(result.ok ? "" : result.error);
              if (result.ok) setSelected([]);
            }}>Import {selected.length ? selected.length + " " : ""}selected as sources</Button>
          </div>
          <div className="table-scroll"><table className="evidence-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Keep</th><th scope="col">Title</th><th scope="col">Employer</th><th scope="col">Location</th><th scope="col">Published</th><th scope="col">Matched</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{postings.map((p) => <tr key={p.id}>
              <td><input type="checkbox" aria-label={"Keep " + p.title} data-demo-id={"collect-select-" + p.id} checked={selected.includes(p.id)} disabled={imported.has(p.id)} onChange={(e) => setSelected(e.target.checked ? [...selected, p.id] : selected.filter((id) => id !== p.id))} /></td>
              <th scope="row">{p.url ? <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{p.title}</a> : p.title}{imported.has(p.id) ? <> <Tag>Imported</Tag></> : null}</th>
              <td>{p.organisation}</td><td>{p.location || "Not stated"}</td><td className="tabular">{p.publishedAt ? p.publishedAt.slice(0, 10) : "Not supplied"}</td>
              <td>{matchedKeywords(p, keywords).join(", ") || (keywords.length ? "text only" : "all")}</td>
            </tr>)}</tbody>
          </table></div>
        </> : <p>No posting matched. Widen the keywords or search inside the text.</p>}
      </div> : null}
    </> : <p className="muted">Only assigned lecturers and coordinators can run a collection for this course.</p>}
  </section>;
}

export function RequirementScan({ state, subject, mayEdit }: Props) {
  const saved = state.skillLexicon[subject.id] ?? [];
  const [terms, setTerms] = useState(saved.join(", "));
  const [ack, setAck] = useState(false);
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const [levels, setLevels] = useState<Record<string, MentionRequirement>>({});
  const proposals = state.scanProposals.filter((p) => state.evidenceSources.some((s) => s.id === p.sourceId && s.subjectId === subject.id));
  const key = (p: MentionProposal) => p.sourceId + "\n" + p.term;
  const postings = state.evidenceSources.filter((s) => s.subjectId === subject.id && s.kind === "job-posting" && !s.duplicateOf);
  const unreviewed = postings.filter((s) => !s.reviewed);
  const dirty = JSON.stringify(parseLexicon(terms)) !== JSON.stringify(saved);
  useUnsavedEditor(dirty);
  const withLevel = (p: MentionProposal) => ({ ...p, requirement: levels[key(p)] ?? p.requirement });
  return <section className="workspace-panel" aria-labelledby="requirement-scan">
    <div className="section-heading"><div><h3 id="requirement-scan">Scan for requirements</h3><p className="muted">Name the skills you care about. The scan proposes the sentence in each posting that uses a term; you confirm every quotation.</p></div></div>
    {mayEdit ? <>
      <Field label="Skills to look for" hint="Comma-separated. Use | for an alias, for example machine learning|ML. Matching is whole-word and case-insensitive."><Textarea data-demo-id="lexicon-terms" value={terms} onChange={(e) => setTerms(e.target.value)} placeholder="e.g. SQL, Python, dashboards|dashboard, data visualisation, stakeholders|stakeholder" /></Field>
      <div className="button-row">
        <Button data-demo-id="lexicon-save" disabled={!dirty} onClick={() => { const result = setSkillLexicon(subject.id, parseLexicon(terms)); setMessage(result.ok ? "Terms saved with the course." : result.error); }}>Save terms</Button>
        <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="scan-run" disabled={dirty || !saved.length || !postings.length} onClick={() => {
          const result = scanForRequirements(subject.id);
          setMessage(result.ok ? result.count + " proposals across " + postings.length + " postings. Confirm the quotations you accept." : result.error);
          setLevels({});
        }}>Scan postings</Button>
      </div>
      {message ? <p role="status" className="save-status">{message}</p> : null}
      {proposals.length ? <>
        <div className="table-scroll"><table className="evidence-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Posting</th><th scope="col">Skill</th><th scope="col">Proposed quotation</th><th scope="col">Requirement</th><th scope="col">Decision</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{proposals.map((p) => <tr key={key(p)}>
            <th scope="row">{p.sourceTitle}</th><td>{p.skill}</td><td><blockquote className="proposal-quote">{p.excerpt}</blockquote></td>
            <td><Select aria-label={"Requirement level for " + p.skill + " in " + p.sourceTitle} value={levels[key(p)] ?? p.requirement} onChange={(e) => setLevels({ ...levels, [key(p)]: e.target.value as MentionRequirement })}>{REQUIREMENT_LEVELS.map((r) => <option key={r} value={r}>{r}</option>)}</Select></td>
            <td><div className="button-row"><Button onClick={() => confirmProposals(subject.id, [withLevel(p)])}>Confirm</Button><Button variant="quiet" onClick={() => dismissProposal(p.sourceId, p.term)}>Dismiss</Button></div></td>
          </tr>)}</tbody>
        </table></div>
        <div className="button-row">
          <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="scan-confirm-all" onClick={() => { const result = confirmProposals(subject.id, proposals.map(withLevel)); setMessage(result.added + " quotations recorded, " + result.skipped + " skipped."); }}>Confirm all {proposals.length}</Button>
          <Button onClick={() => clearProposals()}>Dismiss all</Button>
        </div>
      </> : null}
      {postings.length ? <div className="curriculum-object"><h4>Reviewed denominator</h4>
        <p className="muted">{postings.length - unreviewed.length} of {postings.length} postings are marked reviewed. A posting counts only after you confirm its extraction is complete.</p>
        {unreviewed.length ? <>
          <label className="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" data-demo-id="review-all-ack" checked={ack} onChange={(e) => setAck(e.target.checked)} />I have checked the quotations for these {unreviewed.length} postings, or deliberately skipped what the course does not need.</label>
          <Button data-demo-id="review-all" disabled={!ack} onClick={() => { setSourcesReviewed(subject.id, unreviewed.map((s) => s.id), true); setAck(false); }}>Mark {unreviewed.length} postings reviewed</Button>
        </> : <p className="muted">All postings are reviewed. Unmark one from its card below if you need to revisit it.</p>}
      </div> : null}
    </> : null}
  </section>;
}

export function MeetingBriefPanel({ state, person, subject, mayEdit }: Props) {
  const [recommendation, setRecommendation] = useState<BriefRecommendation>("undecided");
  const [notes, setNotes] = useState("");
  const [recipients, setRecipients] = useState<string[]>([]);
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const briefs = state.evidenceBriefs.filter((b) => b.subjectId === subject.id).reverse();
  const current = briefs.find((b) => b.id === state.selectedBriefId) ?? briefs[0];
  const others = state.people.filter((p) => p.id !== person.id);
  const name = (id: string) => state.people.find((p) => p.id === id)?.name ?? id;
  useUnsavedEditor(Boolean(notes.trim()));
  return <section className="workspace-panel" aria-labelledby="meeting-brief" data-demo-id="meeting-brief">
    <div className="section-heading"><div><h3 id="meeting-brief">Meeting brief</h3><p className="muted">Turn the evidence into a document you can bring to a programme meeting, or send it to a colleague in Lyceum.</p></div></div>
    {mayEdit ? <>
      <div className="form-grid"><Field label="Your recommendation"><Select data-demo-id="brief-recommendation" value={recommendation} onChange={(e) => setRecommendation(e.target.value as BriefRecommendation)}>{(Object.keys(RECOMMENDATION_LABEL) as BriefRecommendation[]).map((r) => <option key={r} value={r}>{RECOMMENDATION_LABEL[r]}</option>)}</Select></Field></div>
      <Field label="Notes for the meeting" hint="What you propose, what it costs in hours, and what you want decided."><Textarea data-demo-id="brief-notes" value={notes} onChange={(e) => setNotes(e.target.value)} /></Field>
      <div className="button-row"><Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="brief-prepare" onClick={() => {
        const result = prepareEvidenceBrief(subject.id, { recommendation, notes });
        setMessage(result.ok ? "Brief prepared from the current evidence. Review it, then download or send it." : result.error);
        if (result.ok) setNotes("");
      }}>Prepare brief</Button></div>
      {message ? <p role="status" className="save-status">{message}</p> : null}
    </> : null}
    {current ? <article className="curriculum-object" data-demo-id="brief-current">
      <div className="section-heading"><div><h4>{RECOMMENDATION_LABEL[current.recommendation]}</h4>
        <p className="muted">Prepared {current.createdAt} by {name(current.createdBy)}{current.sentAt ? " · sent " + current.sentAt + " to " + current.recipients.map(name).join(", ") : " · not sent"}</p></div>
        <div className="button-row">
          <Button data-demo-id="brief-download" onClick={() => downloadText(subject.id + "-meeting-brief.md", current.markdown)}>Download brief (.md)</Button>
          <Button data-demo-id="brief-slides" onClick={() => { const outcomes = state.clos.filter((c) => c.subjectId === subject.id); void downloadDeck(briefDeck(subject, current, evidenceReport(subject.id, state.evidenceSources, state.skillMentions, state.skillMappings, outcomes), state.evidenceSources, state.skillMentions, outcomes, state.people, nowIso())); }}>Download slides (.pptx)</Button>
          {briefs.length > 1 ? <Select aria-label="Choose a prepared brief" value={current.id} onChange={(e) => selectBrief(e.target.value)}>{briefs.map((b) => <option key={b.id} value={b.id}>{b.createdAt} · {RECOMMENDATION_LABEL[b.recommendation]}</option>)}</Select> : null}
        </div></div>
      {current.notes ? <p className="preserve-lines">{current.notes}</p> : null}
      <p className="muted">The slide deck is generated from the current evidence and this brief's recommendation: decision, evidence base, table, coverage, options, limitations and one receipt slide per source. Editable in PowerPoint; no AI-written text.</p>
      <details><summary>Read the full brief</summary><pre className="brief-body">{current.markdown}</pre></details>
      {mayEdit && !current.sentAt ? <fieldset className="clo-choices"><legend>Send to</legend>
        {others.map((p) => <label key={p.id}><input type="checkbox" data-demo-id={"brief-recipient-" + p.id} checked={recipients.includes(p.id)} onChange={(e) => setRecipients(e.target.checked ? [...recipients, p.id] : recipients.filter((id) => id !== p.id))} /><span>{p.name} · {p.orgRole}</span></label>)}
        <div className="button-row"><Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="brief-send" disabled={!recipients.length} onClick={() => {
          const result = sendEvidenceBrief(current.id, recipients);
          setMessage(result.ok ? "Brief sent. Recipients see it on their Home page with the receipts attached." : result.error);
          if (result.ok) setRecipients([]);
        }}>Send brief</Button></div>
        <p className="muted">Sending notifies colleagues inside this local prototype. It is not an institutional submission.</p>
      </fieldset> : null}
    </article> : <p className="muted">No brief prepared yet. Record evidence above, then prepare one.</p>}
  </section>;
}
// The Course Studio (spec 6.3 / 6.4): the centrepiece. Subject editing, the
// review chain, and the assessment studio, kept calm with three quiet tabs so
// density stays opt-in. Works for every role that can reach it: the status and
// the person's hats decide which single primary action is on offer.

import { useState } from "react";
import { can, hatsOn, subjectsForPerson } from "../../app/roles.ts";
import {
  approveTestDraft,
  acknowledgeAssessmentCourseChange,
  resetAssessmentOutcomeWeights,
  canRunTest,
  createTestDraft,
  currentPerson,
  draftWithAgent,
  editCloChangeText,
  editDraftField,
  generateTestItems,
  navigate,
  personById,
  personWithHat,
  removeTestItem,
  requestAgentReview,
  reviewApprove,
  reviewRequestChanges,
  setCritique,
  selectSubject,
  selectStudioTab,
  startAcceptanceRun,
  startDraft,
  submitForReview,
  submitTestDraft,
  testDraftById,
  updateBlueprint,
  updateTestItem,
  useStore,
  type AppState,
} from "../../app/store.ts";
import type {
  BloomLevel,
  ChangeProposal,
  Person,
  ProposalEvent,
  ProposalStatus,
  Subject,
  TestDraft,
} from "../../types.ts";
import { AgentStrip } from "../shell/AgentStrip.tsx";
import { CurriculumPanel, CurriculumHistoryPanel } from "./CurriculumWorkspace.tsx";
import { EvidencePanel } from "./EvidenceWorkspace.tsx";
import { CourseOverview, TeachingPlanPanel } from "./CourseWorkspace.tsx";
import {
  Button,
  Card,
  EmptyState,
  Field,
  Input,
  Page,
  PageHead,
  Row,
  SectionLabel,
  Select,
  Tag,
  Textarea,
} from "../primitives/index.tsx";

const STATUS_LABEL: Record<ProposalStatus, string> = {
  drafting: "Drafting",
  "coordinator-review": "Coordinator review",
  testing: "Ready to test",
  "management-approval": "Awaiting management",
  approved: "Approved",
  rejected: "Rejected",
};

const STATUS_TONE: Record<ProposalStatus, "neutral" | "accent" | "ok" | "warn" | "danger"> = {
  drafting: "neutral",
  "coordinator-review": "warn",
  testing: "accent",
  "management-approval": "accent",
  approved: "ok",
  rejected: "danger",
};

const ACTION_LABEL: Record<ProposalEvent["action"], string> = {
  drafted: "Draft started",
  "agent-drafted": "Agent drafted",
  "agent-reviewed": "Agent reviewed",
  "submitted-for-review": "Submitted for review",
  "review-approved": "Review approved",
  "review-changes-requested": "Changes requested",
  tested: "Acceptance test run",
  approved: "Approved",
  rejected: "Rejected",
};

function fmtWhen(iso: string): string {
  const d = new Date(iso);
  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return iso;
  return d.toLocaleDateString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric" });
}

type TabId = AppState["studioTab"];
const STUDIO_TABS: { id: TabId; label: string }[] = [
  { id: "overview", label: "Overview" }, { id: "curriculum", label: "Outcomes & topics" }, { id: "evidence", label: "Evidence" }, { id: "plan", label: "Teaching plan" },
  { id: "content", label: "Proposal" }, { id: "assessment", label: "Assessment" },
  { id: "history", label: "History" },
];

export function StudioScreen() {
  const state = useStore();
  const person = currentPerson();
  if (!person) return null;
  const ownIds = subjectsForPerson(person.id, state.assignments);
  const subjects = state.subjects.filter((s) => person.orgRole !== "academic" || ownIds.includes(s.id));
  const subject = subjects.find((s) => s.id === state.selectedSubjectId) ?? subjects[0];
  if (!subject) return <Page><PageHead title="Course Studio" context="Your teaching workspace starts with an assigned course." /><EmptyState title="No course assigned yet" body="The department can assign you as a lecturer or coordinator in Assignments. Then your course outcomes, teaching plan and review workspace will appear here." action={<Button onClick={() => navigate("guide")}>Read the section guide</Button>} /></Page>;
  return <StudioCourse key={subject.id + person.id} state={state} person={person} subject={subject} subjects={subjects} />;
}

function StudioCourse({ state, person, subject, subjects }: { state: AppState; person: Person; subject: Subject; subjects: Subject[] }) {
  const tab = state.studioTab;
  const proposal = state.proposals.find((p) => p.subjectId === subject.id && p.status !== "approved" && p.status !== "rejected");
  const lastProposal = [...state.proposals].reverse().find((p) => p.subjectId === subject.id);
  const coordinator = personWithHat(subject.id, "coordinator");
  const mayDraft = can(person, "draft-change", { subjectId: subject.id, assignments: state.assignments });
  return <Page wide>
    <PageHead title={subject.id + " " + subject.title} context={<span>Year {subject.year} · Semester {subject.semester} · Coordinator: {coordinator?.name ?? "unassigned"}</span>} actions={
      <label className="course-switcher">Course<Select aria-label="Choose course" value={subject.id} onChange={(e) => selectSubject(e.target.value)}>{subjects.map((s) => <option key={s.id} value={s.id}>{s.id} · {s.title}</option>)}</Select></label>
    } />
    <div className="course-workspace-meta"><Tag>{subject.workspaceOnly ? "Personal course workspace" : subject.status === "proposed" ? "Proposed course" : "Course workspace"}</Tag><span role="status">{state.persistenceStatus === "unavailable" ? "Browser storage unavailable. Export your plan before closing." : state.persistenceStatus === "pending" ? "Saving in this browser…" : "Changes stored in this browser"}</span></div>
    <div className="studio-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Course workspace">
      {STUDIO_TABS.map((item, index) => <button key={item.id} role="tab" id={"studio-tab-" + item.id} aria-controls={"studio-panel-" + item.id} aria-selected={tab === item.id} tabIndex={tab === item.id ? 0 : -1} data-demo-id={"tab-" + item.id} onClick={() => selectStudioTab(item.id)} onKeyDown={(event) => {
        const keys = ["ArrowRight", "ArrowLeft", "Home", "End"];
        if (!keys.includes(event.key)) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        const next = event.key === "Home" ? 0 : event.key === "End" ? STUDIO_TABS.length - 1 : (index + (event.key === "ArrowRight" ? 1 : -1) + STUDIO_TABS.length) % STUDIO_TABS.length;
        selectStudioTab(STUDIO_TABS[next].id);
        document.getElementById("studio-tab-" + STUDIO_TABS[next].id)?.focus();
      }}>{item.label}</button>)}
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-overview" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-overview" hidden={tab !== "overview"} tabIndex={0}>
      <CourseOverview state={state} person={person} subject={subject} proposal={proposal} onCurriculum={() => selectStudioTab("curriculum")} onEvidence={() => selectStudioTab("evidence")} onPlan={() => selectStudioTab("plan")} onProposal={() => selectStudioTab("content")} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-curriculum" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-curriculum" hidden={tab !== "curriculum"} tabIndex={0}>
      <CurriculumPanel state={state} person={person} subject={subject} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-evidence" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-evidence" hidden={tab !== "evidence"} tabIndex={0}>
      <EvidencePanel state={state} person={person} subject={subject} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-plan" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-plan" hidden={tab !== "plan"} tabIndex={0}>
      <TeachingPlanPanel state={state} person={person} subject={subject} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-content" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-content" hidden={tab !== "content"} tabIndex={0}>
      {proposal ? <><div className="section-heading"><h2>Curriculum change proposal</h2><Tag tone={STATUS_TONE[proposal.status]}>{STATUS_LABEL[proposal.status]}</Tag></div><ContentTab key={proposal.id} state={state} person={person} subject={subject} proposal={proposal} /></> : <section className="workspace-panel"><h2>Plan a formal curriculum change</h2><p>A proposal holds the topic and outcome changes you want the coordinator and management to review. Your teaching plan can be prepared independently.</p>{lastProposal ? <p className="limitation">The previous proposal is {lastProposal.status}. Legacy proposal approval is a separate prototype workflow. Use Outcomes & topics for a lecturer-controlled course revision.</p> : null}{subject.workspaceOnly ? <Button variant="primary" onClick={() => selectStudioTab("curriculum")}>Open Outcomes & topics</Button> : mayDraft ? <Button variant="primary" data-demo-id="studio-start-draft" onClick={() => startDraft(subject.id)}>Start a draft</Button> : <p className="muted">Only an assigned lecturer or coordinator can draft a change.</p>}</section>}
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-assessment" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-assessment" hidden={tab !== "assessment"} tabIndex={0}>
      <AssessmentTab state={state} person={person} subject={subject} proposal={proposal} />
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="studio-panel-history" aria-labelledby="studio-tab-history" hidden={tab !== "history"} tabIndex={0}>
      <CurriculumHistoryPanel state={state} subject={subject} />
      {lastProposal ? <HistoryTab state={state} subject={subject} proposal={proposal ?? lastProposal} /> : <section className="workspace-panel"><h2>Course history</h2><p>No proposal events are recorded yet. Starting a proposal creates its first event; teaching-session edits are saved separately in your plan.</p><p className="muted">Current version: {subject.currentVersionId}</p></section>}
    </div>
  </Page>;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Content: the draft, editable in place, with the agent modes, the critique,
// and the one status-driven primary action.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

function ContentTab(props: {
  state: AppState;
  person: Person;
  subject: Subject;
  proposal: ChangeProposal;
}) {
  const { state, person, subject, proposal } = props;
  const [mode, setMode] = useState<"self" | "agent" | "hybrid">("self");
  const [changesOpen, setChangesOpen] = useState(false);
  const [changeNote, setChangeNote] = useState("");

  const hats = hatsOn(person.id, subject.id, state.assignments);
  const coordHere = hats.includes("coordinator");
  const isAuthor = proposal.authorId === person.id;
  const mayReview =
    proposal.status === "coordinator-review" &&
    can(person, "review-draft", { subjectId: subject.id, assignments: state.assignments });

  // The topics textarea is uncontrolled (the store normalises lines, which would
  // eat newlines mid-typing); it remounts whenever the agent rewrites the draft.
  const agentDraftCount = proposal.history.filter((h) => h.action === "agent-drafted").length;
  const topicsKey = `${proposal.id}-topics-${agentDraftCount}`;

  const draft = proposal.draft;

  function pickMode(next: "self" | "agent" | "hybrid") {
    setMode(next);
    if (next === "agent" || next === "hybrid") draftWithAgent(proposal.id, next);
  }

  const modeButton = (id: "self" | "agent" | "hybrid", label: string) => (
    <Button
      variant="outline"
      data-demo-id={`mode-${id}`}
      onClick={() => pickMode(id)}
      style={{
        height: 30,
        padding: "0 12px",
        fontSize: 13,
        ...(mode === id
          ? {
              borderColor: "var(--accent)",
              color: "var(--accent)",
              background: "var(--accent-soft)",
            }
          : {}),
      }}
    >
      {label}
    </Button>
  );

  return (
    <div>
      <AgentStrip
        agent="authoring"
        idleText="Authoring drafts, reviews, and fixes. Pick a mode or ask for a review."
      />

      {mayReview ? (
        <Card focal style={{ marginBottom: 20 }}>
          <div style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 15, marginBottom: 4 }}>
            A lecturer's draft awaits your review
          </div>
          <p style={{ margin: "0 0 14px", fontSize: 13.5, color: "var(--ink-2)", maxWidth: 560 }}>
            Approve it for testing, or send it back with a note. Nothing reaches the acceptance
            test without your review.
          </p>
          <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 10 }}>
            <Button
              variant="primary"
              data-demo-id="review-approve"
              onClick={() => reviewApprove(proposal.id)}
            >
              Approve for testing
            </Button>
            <Button
              variant="quiet"
              data-demo-id="review-changes"
              onClick={() => setChangesOpen((v) => !v)}
            >
              Request changes
            </Button>
          </div>
          {changesOpen ? (
            <div style={{ marginTop: 12 }}>
              <Textarea
                value={changeNote}
                onChange={(e) => setChangeNote(e.target.value)}
                placeholder="What should change before this is tested?"
                style={{ minHeight: 64 }}
              />
              <Button
                variant="outline"
                style={{ marginTop: 8 }}
                onClick={() => {
                  reviewRequestChanges(proposal.id, changeNote.trim());
                  setChangesOpen(false);
                  setChangeNote("");
                }}
              >
                Send back to the author
              </Button>
            </div>
          ) : null}
        </Card>
      ) : null}

      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Drafting mode</SectionLabel>
      <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, marginBottom: 18 }}>
        {modeButton("self", "Self")}
        {modeButton("agent", "Agent drafts")}
        {modeButton("hybrid", "Hybrid")}
      </div>

      <Field label="Topics" hint="One topic per line.">
        <Textarea
          key={topicsKey}
          defaultValue={(draft.topics ?? []).join("\n")}
          onChange={(e) => editDraftField(proposal.id, "topics", e.target.value)}
          style={{ minHeight: 104 }}
        />
      </Field>

      <SectionLabel>Outcome changes</SectionLabel>
      {(draft.cloChanges ?? []).length === 0 ? (
        <EmptyState
          title="No outcome changes yet"
          body="Agent or hybrid mode drafts an edit to this subject's outcomes; you can refine every line."
        />
      ) : (
        (draft.cloChanges ?? []).map((c, i) => (
          <div
            key={`${c.cloId ?? "new"}-${i}`}
            style={{
              border: "1px solid var(--border)",
              borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
              padding: 12,
              marginBottom: 10,
              background: "var(--surface)",
            }}
          >
            <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 6, marginBottom: 8 }}>
              <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12.5, fontWeight: 600, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
                {c.cloId ?? "new outcome"}
              </span>
              <Tag tone={c.op === "remove" ? "danger" : c.op === "add" ? "ok" : "accent"}>{c.op}</Tag>
              <Tag>{c.bloomLevel}</Tag>
            </div>
            <Textarea
              data-demo-id={i === 0 ? "studio-draft-clo-0" : undefined}
              value={c.text}
              onChange={(e) => editCloChangeText(proposal.id, i, e.target.value)}
              style={{ minHeight: 64 }}
            />
          </div>
        ))
      )}

      <Field label="Test notes">
        <Textarea
          value={draft.testDraft ?? ""}
          onChange={(e) => editDraftField(proposal.id, "testDraft", e.target.value)}
          style={{ minHeight: 72 }}
        />
      </Field>
      <Field label="Lab notes">
        <Textarea
          value={draft.labDraft ?? ""}
          onChange={(e) => editDraftField(proposal.id, "labDraft", e.target.value)}
          style={{ minHeight: 72 }}
        />
      </Field>

      <div style={{ margin: "4px 0 16px" }}>
        <Button variant="quiet" onClick={() => requestAgentReview(proposal.id)}>
          Ask the agent to review
        </Button>
      </div>

      {state.critique ? (
        <div
          style={{
            background: "var(--warn-soft)",
            borderRadius: "var(--radius-s)",
            padding: "10px 12px",
            marginBottom: 18,
          }}
        >
          <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", justifyContent: "space-between" }}>
            <span style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13, color: "var(--warn)" }}>
              The agent's review
            </span>
            <Button
              variant="quiet"
              style={{ height: 24, padding: "0 8px", fontSize: 12 }}
              onClick={() => setCritique(null)}
            >
              Dismiss
            </Button>
          </div>
          <ul style={{ margin: "6px 0 0", paddingLeft: 18 }}>
            {state.critique.map((line, i) => (
              <li key={i} style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)", marginBottom: 2 }}>
                {line}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ) : null}

      {/* The one status-driven primary action. */}
      {isAuthor && !coordHere && proposal.status === "drafting" ? (
        <Button
          variant="primary"
          data-demo-id="studio-submit-review"
          onClick={() => submitForReview(proposal.id)}
        >
          Submit for coordinator review
        </Button>
      ) : canRunTest(proposal.id) ? (
        <Button
          variant="primary"
          data-demo-id="studio-run-test"
          onClick={() => startAcceptanceRun(proposal.id)}
        >
          Run the acceptance test
        </Button>
      ) : null}

      {proposal.status === "management-approval" ? (
        <div style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
          Tested. Awaiting management.{" "}
          <a
            href="#"
            onClick={(e) => {
              e.preventDefault();
              navigate("acceptance");
            }}
          >
            View the acceptance run
          </a>
        </div>
      ) : null}
      {proposal.status === "approved" ? (
        <div style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ok)" }}>
          Live. The prediction is recorded.{" "}
          <a
            href="#"
            onClick={(e) => {
              e.preventDefault();
              navigate("backtest");
            }}
          >
            See the closed loop
          </a>
        </div>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Assessment: the blueprint, agent-drafted items, the coverage meter, and the
// same review chain as the proposal (spec 6.4).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

const MIX_LEVELS: BloomLevel[] = ["Understand", "Apply", "Analyse"];

function AssessmentTab(props: {
  state: AppState;
  person: Person;
  subject: Subject;
  proposal?: ChangeProposal;
}) {
  const { state, person, subject, proposal } = props;
  const [selectedId,setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null);
  const tests = state.testDrafts.filter(t => t.subjectId === subject.id);
  const td = tests.find(t => t.id === selectedId) ?? testDraftById(proposal?.draft.testDraftId) ?? tests.at(-1);

  if (!td) {
    return (
      <EmptyState
        title="No test draft yet"
        body="Prepare a blueprint for this course. Local templates can draft example questions; review every task and mark allocation before using them. An assessment can be prepared without a curriculum proposal."
        action={
          <Button
            variant="primary"
            data-demo-id="assessment-start"
            onClick={() => createTestDraft(subject.id, proposal?.id)}
          >
            Start a test draft
          </Button>
        }
      />
    );
  }

  const weightSum = td.blueprint.cloWeights.reduce((s, w) => s + w.weight, 0);
  const mixSum = Object.values(td.blueprint.bloomMix).reduce<number>((s, v) => s + (v ?? 0), 0);
  const weightsOk = Math.abs(weightSum - 1) <= 0.01;
  const mixOk = mixSum <= 1;
  const hasItems = td.items.length > 0;

  return (
    <div>
      <Field label="Assessment draft"><Select value={td.id} onChange={e => setSelectedId(e.target.value)}>{tests.map(t => <option key={t.id} value={t.id}>{t.id} · {t.needsReview ? "Review course change" : t.status}</option>)}</Select></Field>
      <p className="limitation">Question generation uses local wording templates. It does not establish assessment quality; exact mark-allocation and task/rubric generation remain under development.</p>

      {td.needsReview ? <section className="workspace-panel">
        <h3>Review course change</h3>
        <p className="limitation">The course changed. Your questions are preserved; review their wording, outcome links, weights and marks before submitting again.</p>
        <Button onClick={() => resetAssessmentOutcomeWeights(td.id)}>Reset weights to current outcomes</Button>
        <p className="muted">This replaces the outcome weights with equal weights and keeps your questions. Remove questions linked to retired outcomes or draft new items, then adjust the weights.</p>
      </section> : null}

      {/* (a) the blueprint, editable */}
      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Blueprint</SectionLabel>
      <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginBottom: 12 }}>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, width: 130, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>Total marks</span>
        <Input
          type="number"
          min={1}
          className="num"
          style={{ width: 90 }}
          aria-label="Total assessment marks"
          value={td.blueprint.totalMarks}
          onChange={(e) =>
            updateBlueprint(td.id, { ...td.blueprint, totalMarks: Number(e.target.value) })
          }
        />
      </div>
      {td.blueprint.cloWeights.map((cw) => {
        const clo = state.clos.find((c) => c.id === cw.cloId);
        return (
          <div
            key={cw.cloId}
            style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginBottom: 8 }}
          >
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 13, width: 130, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              {cw.cloId} weight
            </span>
            <Input
              type="number"
              min={0}
              max={1}
              step={0.05}
              className="num"
              style={{ width: 90 }}
              aria-label={(clo?.label ?? cw.cloId) + " weight"}
              value={cw.weight}
              onChange={(e) =>
                updateBlueprint(td.id, {
                  ...td.blueprint,
                  cloWeights: td.blueprint.cloWeights.map((w) =>
                    w.cloId === cw.cloId ? { ...w, weight: Number(e.target.value) } : w,
                  ),
                })
              }
            />
            <span style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>{clo?.text ?? cw.cloId}</span>
          </div>
        );
      })}
      <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginTop: 12 }}>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, width: 130, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>Bloom mix</span>
        {MIX_LEVELS.map((level) => (
          <span key={level} style={{ display: "inline-flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 6 }}>
            <Input
              type="number"
              min={0}
              max={1}
              step={0.05}
              className="num"
              style={{ width: 74 }}
              aria-label={level + " share"}
              value={td.blueprint.bloomMix[level] ?? 0}
              onChange={(e) =>
                updateBlueprint(td.id, {
                  ...td.blueprint,
                  bloomMix: { ...td.blueprint.bloomMix, [level]: Number(e.target.value) },
                })
              }
            />
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>{level}</span>
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 8, margin: "14px 0 20px" }}>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-3)" }}>Blueprint check</span>
        <Tag tone={weightsOk ? "ok" : "danger"}>
          <span className="num">weights {weightSum.toFixed(2)}</span>
        </Tag>
        <Tag tone={mixOk ? "ok" : "danger"}>
          <span className="num">bloom mix {mixSum.toFixed(2)}</span>
        </Tag>
      </div>

      {/* (b) generation + (c) the items */}
      {hasItems ? (
        <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 10, marginBottom: 14 }}>
          <SectionLabel style={{ margin: 0 }}>Items</SectionLabel>
          <span style={{ flex: 1 }} />
          <Button
            variant="outline"
            data-demo-id="assessment-generate"
            onClick={() => generateTestItems(td.id)}
          >
            Draft items against the blueprint
          </Button>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <EmptyState
          title="No items yet"
          body="Local templates draft example wording from current outcomes. Review the questions, coverage and marks; every item stays editable."
          action={
            <Button
              variant="primary"
              data-demo-id="assessment-generate"
              onClick={() => generateTestItems(td.id)}
            >
              Draft items against the blueprint
            </Button>
          }
        />
      )}

      {td.items.map((it, idx) => (
        <Card key={it.id} style={{ marginBottom: 10, boxShadow: "none" }}>
          <div style={{ display: "flex", flexWrap: "wrap", alignItems: "center", gap: 8, marginBottom: 8 }}>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13 }}>
              Q{idx + 1}
            </span>
            <Tag>{it.bloomLevel}</Tag>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              {it.targetCLO}
            </span>
            {it.source === "human" ? <Tag>edited</Tag> : null}
            <span style={{ flex: 1 }} />
            <Input
              type="number"
              min={1}
              className="num"
              style={{ width: 70 }}
              aria-label={"Question " + (idx + 1) + " marks"}
              value={it.marks}
              onChange={(e) => updateTestItem(td.id, it.id, { marks: Number(e.target.value) })}
            />
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-3)" }}>marks</span>
            <Button
              variant="quiet"
              style={{ height: 28, padding: "0 8px", fontSize: 12.5 }}
              aria-label={"Remove question " + (idx + 1)}
              onClick={() => removeTestItem(td.id, it.id)}
            >
              Remove
            </Button>
          </div>
          <Textarea
            aria-label={"Question " + (idx + 1) + " wording"}
            value={it.text}
            onChange={(e) => updateTestItem(td.id, it.id, { text: e.target.value })}
            style={{ minHeight: 56 }}
          />
        </Card>
      ))}

      {/* (d) coverage meter */}
      {hasItems ? <CoverageMeter draft={td} /> : null}

      {/* (e) status action: exactly one primary at a time. */}
      {hasItems ? (
        <div style={{ marginTop: 20 }}>
          <TestStatusAction state={state} person={person} subject={subject} draft={td} />
        </div>
      ) : null}
    </div>
  );
}

function CoverageMeter(props: { draft: TestDraft }) {
  const td = props.draft;
  const totalMarks = td.items.reduce((s, it) => s + it.marks, 0);
  const itemLevels = [...new Set<BloomLevel>([...MIX_LEVELS, ...td.items.map((it) => it.bloomLevel)])];

  const bar = (value: number, color: string) => (
    <div
      style={{
        height: 4,
        background: "var(--surface-2)",
        borderRadius: 2,
        marginTop: 3,
        maxWidth: 360,
      }}
    >
      <div
        style={{
          width: `${Math.min(100, Math.max(0, value * 100)).toFixed(1)}%`,
          height: "100%",
          background: color,
          borderRadius: 2,
        }}
      />
    </div>
  );

  return (
    <div style={{ marginTop: 20 }}>
      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Coverage against the blueprint</SectionLabel>
      {td.blueprint.cloWeights.map((cw) => {
        const actual =
          totalMarks > 0
            ? td.items.filter((it) => it.targetCLO === cw.cloId).reduce((s, it) => s + it.marks, 0) /
              totalMarks
            : 0;
        return (
          <div key={cw.cloId} style={{ marginBottom: 10 }}>
            <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              <span className="num" style={{ width: 48, fontWeight: 600 }}>
                {cw.cloId}
              </span>
              <span className="num">
                {(actual * 100).toFixed(0)}% of marks, planned {(cw.weight * 100).toFixed(0)}%
              </span>
            </div>
            {bar(actual, "var(--accent)")}
            {bar(cw.weight, "var(--border)")}
          </div>
        );
      })}
      {itemLevels.map((level) => {
        const share =
          td.items.length > 0
            ? td.items.filter((it) => it.bloomLevel === level).length / td.items.length
            : 0;
        const target = td.blueprint.bloomMix[level] ?? 0;
        return (
          <div key={level} style={{ marginBottom: 10 }}>
            <div style={{ display: "flex", gap: 8, fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
              <span style={{ width: 90 }}>{level}</span>
              <span className="num">
                {(share * 100).toFixed(0)}% of items, mix {(target * 100).toFixed(0)}%
              </span>
            </div>
            {bar(share, "var(--accent)")}
            {bar(target, "var(--border)")}
          </div>
        );
      })}
    </div>
  );
}

function TestStatusAction(props: {
  state: AppState;
  person: Person;
  subject: Subject;
  draft: TestDraft;
}) {
  const { state, person, subject, draft } = props;

  const [reviewed,setReviewed] = useState(false);
  const [reviewError,setReviewError] = useState("");
  if (draft.needsReview) return <div>
    <label className="checkbox-line"><input type="checkbox" data-demo-id="assessment-course-change-ack" checked={reviewed} onChange={e => setReviewed(e.target.checked)} />I reviewed the blueprint and every question against the current course outcomes.</label>
    <Button data-demo-id="assessment-course-change-review" disabled={!reviewed} onClick={() => {
      const result = acknowledgeAssessmentCourseChange(draft.id,reviewed);
      setReviewError(result.ok ? "" : result.error ?? "The review could not be recorded.");
    }}>Record course-change review</Button>
    {reviewError ? <p role="alert" className="form-error">{reviewError}</p> : null}
  </div>;

  if (draft.status === "approved") {
    return (
      <div style={{ display: "flex", alignItems: "center", gap: 8 }}>
        <Tag tone="ok">Approved</Tag>
        <span style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
          {draft.proposalId ? "This local test decision is attached to the proposal." : "Local assessment decision recorded. Institutional approval remains in your university process."}
        </span>
      </div>
    );
  }

  if (
    draft.status === "coordinator-review" &&
    can(person, "review-draft", { subjectId: subject.id, assignments: state.assignments })
  ) {
    return (
      <Button variant="primary" onClick={() => approveTestDraft(draft.id)}>
        Approve test
      </Button>
    );
  }

  if (draft.status === "coordinator-review") {
    return (
      <span style={{ fontSize: 13, color: "var(--ink-2)" }}>
        Sent for review. Awaiting the coordinator.
      </span>
    );
  }

  // Drafting: the author moves it on. A coordinator's own draft approves
  // directly; a lecturer's goes to the coordinator (both via submitTestDraft).
  if (draft.status === "drafting" && draft.authorId === person.id) {
    const authorIsCoordHere = hatsOn(draft.authorId, subject.id, state.assignments).includes(
      "coordinator",
    );
    return (
      <Button
        variant="primary"
        data-demo-id="assessment-submit"
        onClick={() => submitTestDraft(draft.id)}
      >
        {authorIsCoordHere ? "Approve test" : "Send test for review"}
      </Button>
    );
  }

  return null;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// History: the proposal's events, newest first, then the subject's versions.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

function HistoryTab(props: { state: AppState; subject: Subject; proposal: ChangeProposal }) {
  const { state, subject, proposal } = props;
  const events = [...proposal.history].reverse();
  const versions = [...state.subjectVersions]
    .filter((v) => v.subjectId === subject.id)
    .reverse();

  return (
    <div>
      <SectionLabel style={{ marginTop: 0 }}>Proposal history</SectionLabel>
      {events.length === 0 ? (
        <EmptyState
          title="Nothing has happened yet"
          body="Proposal actions are recorded here. Course revision decisions appear above."
        />
      ) : (
        events.map((e, i) => (
          <Row key={`${e.at}-${e.action}-${i}`}>
            <span style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13, width: 180, flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {ACTION_LABEL[e.action]}
            </span>
            <span
              style={{
                flex: 1,
                fontSize: 13,
                color: "var(--ink-2)",
                overflow: "hidden",
                textOverflow: "ellipsis",
                whiteSpace: "nowrap",
              }}
            >
              {e.note ?? ""}
            </span>
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {personById(e.byPersonId)?.name ?? e.byPersonId}
            </span>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12, color: "var(--ink-3)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {fmtWhen(e.at)}
            </span>
          </Row>
        ))
      )}

      <SectionLabel>Subject versions</SectionLabel>
      {versions.length === 0 ? (
        <EmptyState
          title="No versions yet"
          body="Each approved change snapshots the subject here, so every revision stays traceable."
        />
      ) : (
        versions.map((v) => (
          <Row key={v.id}>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontWeight: 600, fontSize: 13, width: 120, flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {v.id}
            </span>
            <span
              style={{
                flex: 1,
                fontSize: 13,
                color: "var(--ink-2)",
                overflow: "hidden",
                textOverflow: "ellipsis",
                whiteSpace: "nowrap",
              }}
            >
              {v.reason}
            </span>
            <span style={{ fontSize: 12.5, color: "var(--ink-2)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {personById(v.changedBy)?.name ?? v.changedBy}
            </span>
            <span className="num" style={{ fontSize: 12, color: "var(--ink-3)", flexShrink: 0 }}>
              {fmtWhen(v.changedAt)}
            </span>
          </Row>
        ))
      )}
    </div>
  );
}

